1
00:00:13,430 --> 00:00:17,183
WITH THE FINAL CLIMB AROUND THE CORNER,
THEY ARRIVE HERE

2
00:00:17,851 --> 00:00:19,728
THE TRADITIONAL MEDICINE PACKAGE'S
LAST PART

3
00:00:19,811 --> 00:00:21,396
A TRADITIONAL MEDICINE FOOT BATH CAFE

4
00:00:22,022 --> 00:00:25,984
THE FOOT BATHS BEGIN

5
00:00:27,694 --> 00:00:29,988
THEY FIRST FILL THE TUBS WITH WARM WATER

6
00:00:31,239 --> 00:00:32,240
This smells nice.

7
00:00:33,533 --> 00:00:35,326
I guess it'll turn really purple.

8
00:00:35,410 --> 00:00:37,579
FRAGRANT TRADITIONAL MEDICINE
FOOT SOAK IS ADDED

9
00:00:38,121 --> 00:00:40,331
CAREFULLY DIPPING IN
ONE FOOT AT A TIME

10
00:00:40,957 --> 00:00:41,958
It's warm.

11
00:00:42,459 --> 00:00:43,710
It does feel nice.

12
00:00:44,878 --> 00:00:47,297
TIME TO RECOVER FROM FATIGUE
BEFORE THE FINAL HIKE

13
00:00:47,881 --> 00:00:49,966
I'll briefly explain tomorrow's trail.

14
00:00:50,049 --> 00:00:50,925
Okay.

15
00:00:51,009 --> 00:00:55,054
Every February, Jirisan enters
a forest fire precaution period.

16
00:00:55,138 --> 00:00:56,931
ACCESS TO TRAILS ARE RESTRICTED

17
00:00:57,015 --> 00:00:58,433
OR SHUT DOWN EVERY SPRING AND FALL

18
00:00:59,267 --> 00:01:01,269
JIRISAN HAS BEEN RESTRICTED
TO PREVENT FOREST FIRES

19
00:01:01,352 --> 00:01:02,896
So, there are only two trails

20
00:01:03,438 --> 00:01:04,606
that are currently available.

21
00:01:05,148 --> 00:01:07,484
AMONG COUNTLESS RESTRICTED TRAILS IN RED

22
00:01:07,567 --> 00:01:10,904
BAEKMUDONG, CHEONWANGBONG, JUNGSAN

23
00:01:10,987 --> 00:01:13,073
CHEONWANGBONG, JIRISAN

24
00:01:13,156 --> 00:01:15,366
First, the Baekmudong Trail.

25
00:01:15,450 --> 00:01:17,577
Next, the Jungsanri Trail.

26
00:01:18,328 --> 00:01:19,788
There are two trails available.

27
00:01:19,871 --> 00:01:24,209
They both lead to Jangteomok Shelter,

28
00:01:24,292 --> 00:01:27,378
where all four of you will reunite
and climb to Cheonwangbong together.

29
00:01:27,462 --> 00:01:30,131
JANGTEOMOK SHELTER IS LOCATED
ON THE UPPER MIDDLE PART OF JIRISAN

30
00:01:30,215 --> 00:01:34,552
DESCEND CLUB WILL SPLIT UP INTO PAIRS

31
00:01:34,636 --> 00:01:37,347
AND GATHER AT JANGTEOMOK SHELTER

32
00:01:38,765 --> 00:01:42,602
THEY WILL HIKE TOGETHER
TO THE PEAK, CHEONWANGBONG

33
00:01:42,685 --> 00:01:45,772
The Baekmudong Trail
is a bit hard in the beginning.

34
00:01:46,397 --> 00:01:50,235
Then, the second half
to Jangteomok Shelter eases up a little.

35
00:01:51,486 --> 00:01:53,363
BAEKMUDONG TRAIL

36
00:01:56,407 --> 00:01:59,244
DIFFICULTY LEVEL IS HARD AT FIRST

37
00:02:03,248 --> 00:02:05,708
BUT IT BECOMES EASIER LATER ON

38
00:02:05,792 --> 00:02:08,878
AFTER SUFFERING COMES JOY
BAEKMUDONG TRAIL

39
00:02:08,962 --> 00:02:10,713
One is Baekmudong. What's the other one?

40
00:02:10,797 --> 00:02:12,465
-Jungsanri.
-Jungsanri.

41
00:02:12,549 --> 00:02:16,344
With the Jungsanri Trail,
it's moderate at first,

42
00:02:16,427 --> 00:02:18,429
and then the second half
becomes difficult.

43
00:02:18,972 --> 00:02:20,390
JUNGSANRI TRAIL

44
00:02:23,017 --> 00:02:25,854
DIFFICULTY LEVEL IS MODERATE AT FIRST

45
00:02:28,815 --> 00:02:30,733
BUT IT BECOMES VERY HARD LATER ON

46
00:02:32,569 --> 00:02:34,571
GETS WORSE AND WORSE
JUNGSANRI TRAIL

47
00:02:34,654 --> 00:02:38,116
Usually, people find
the Jungsanri trail harder.

48
00:02:38,658 --> 00:02:40,618
AVERAGE GRADIENT IS 22.7%
UNTIL JANGTEOMOK SHELTER

49
00:02:40,702 --> 00:02:41,578
JANGTEOMOK SHELTER

50
00:02:41,661 --> 00:02:43,746
AVERAGE GRADIENT IS 31.8%
PAST BYEONGGIMAKTEO SHELTER

51
00:02:44,414 --> 00:02:46,499
ALTHOUGH EVERYONE HAS A DIFFERENT TAKE
ON THE TRAILS

52
00:02:46,583 --> 00:02:48,501
NOT ALL BUT MOST AGREE
THAT JUNGSANRI IS HARDER

53
00:02:48,585 --> 00:02:50,628
Okay, I'll take the Baekmudong Trail.

54
00:02:50,712 --> 00:02:52,589
I'll take the Baekmudong Trail too.

55
00:02:53,548 --> 00:02:54,382
Jungsanri…

56
00:02:54,465 --> 00:02:55,675
VEHEMENTLY REFUSING JUNGSANRI

57
00:02:55,758 --> 00:02:56,801
We decide, right?

58
00:02:56,885 --> 00:02:57,927
Yes, do as you like.

59
00:02:58,011 --> 00:03:00,680
Since they took
Gwaneumsa trail last time,

60
00:03:00,763 --> 00:03:03,766
we'll take
the more difficult one this time.

61
00:03:03,850 --> 00:03:05,226
-Take the hard but fast one?
-Yes.

62
00:03:05,310 --> 00:03:06,936
CAR-THE AND CHAE-MIN
PICK JUNGSANRI

63
00:03:07,020 --> 00:03:08,479
-So considerate.
-That's so cool.

64
00:03:09,480 --> 00:03:11,232
-That's so cool of them.
-So cool.

65
00:03:11,316 --> 00:03:13,484
DOWOON AND TARZZAN WILL TAKE BAEKMUDONG

66
00:03:13,568 --> 00:03:16,487
The Baekmudong team
will have to leave earlier in the morning.

67
00:03:16,571 --> 00:03:19,949
I can sleep 30 minutes more,
so that's good.

68
00:03:20,033 --> 00:03:23,536
THE JUNGSANRI TEAM
WILL DEPART 30 MINUTES LATER

69
00:03:23,620 --> 00:03:25,496
Okay, Team Heartthrobs and Team Uggo.

70
00:03:26,456 --> 00:03:28,541
"Uggo" is such an outdated term.

71
00:03:28,625 --> 00:03:30,043
AND SO, THE TEAMS WERE FORMED

72
00:03:31,210 --> 00:03:33,254
DOWOON AND TARZZAN
THE BAEKMUDONG TEAM UGGOS

73
00:03:33,338 --> 00:03:35,757
CAR, THE GARDEN AND CHAE-MIN
THE JUNGSANRI TEAM HEARTTHROBS

74
00:03:39,344 --> 00:03:41,638
THE SUN SETS BEHIND JIRISAN

75
00:03:43,097 --> 00:03:46,434
THE LAST MORNING COMES

76
00:03:47,060 --> 00:03:49,604
CURRENT TIME

77
00:03:51,314 --> 00:03:53,483
Let's do this, Jung-won.
Today is the last day!

78
00:03:55,235 --> 00:03:57,487
DOWOON IS EXCITED FOR THE LAST HIKE

79
00:04:00,114 --> 00:04:02,784
THE CAMERA OPERATOR SUFFERED WITH HIM
AND HE PATS HIS SHOULDER

80
00:04:04,619 --> 00:04:07,997
HE STARTS TAPPING HIS POLES RHYTHMICALLY

81
00:04:08,081 --> 00:04:10,041
You might discover
the true joy of hiking today

82
00:04:10,124 --> 00:04:11,459
since you'll be free of burden.

83
00:04:11,542 --> 00:04:14,170
-Today will be the most fun.
-Exactly.

84
00:04:14,254 --> 00:04:16,130
Today's hike will be the most fun.

85
00:04:16,214 --> 00:04:18,091
I should do this when I descend.

86
00:04:19,092 --> 00:04:20,301
Almost like skiing.

87
00:04:20,802 --> 00:04:22,553
If it's just like the Yeongnam Alps…

88
00:04:22,637 --> 00:04:24,013
What are you doing? Let's go!

89
00:04:24,097 --> 00:04:25,098
Let's go!

90
00:04:26,557 --> 00:04:27,767
Bye.

91
00:04:27,850 --> 00:04:30,228
THE MOST ENERGETIC START TO DATE

92
00:04:34,107 --> 00:04:36,943
THE BAEKMUDONG TEAM DEPARTS BASE CAMP

93
00:04:37,819 --> 00:04:40,029
Yeah, you have to hike
in a good mood like this.

94
00:04:40,697 --> 00:04:42,031
Gosh, I'm so happy.

95
00:04:43,741 --> 00:04:46,661
THEY RIDE ON HAPPILY FOR 1 HOUR

96
00:04:46,744 --> 00:04:50,665
197-3, GANGCHEONG-RI, MACHEON-MYEON,
HAMYANG-GUN, SOUTH GYEONGSANG PROVINCE

97
00:04:50,748 --> 00:04:53,001
JIRISAN, HAMYANG

98
00:04:53,626 --> 00:04:54,752
It's cold.

99
00:04:55,712 --> 00:04:57,046
It's cold, Dowoon.

100
00:04:57,130 --> 00:04:58,715
HIS BREATH FOGS AS HE LETS OUT A LAUGH

101
00:04:59,841 --> 00:05:02,343
CURRENT TEMPERATURE: -2.1℃

102
00:05:02,969 --> 00:05:04,637
It's good thing we wore padded jackets.

103
00:05:07,265 --> 00:05:11,019
EVEN IN MARCH,
YOU NEED PADDED JACKETS HERE

104
00:05:12,854 --> 00:05:16,899
JIRISAN'S BAEKMUDONG TRAIL

105
00:05:17,734 --> 00:05:21,112
DISTANCE TO JANGTEOMOK SHELTER

106
00:05:21,195 --> 00:05:23,072
BAENGMUDONG INFORMATION CENTER

107
00:05:23,156 --> 00:05:27,076
HARD DIFFICULTY

108
00:05:27,160 --> 00:05:29,120
CHAMSAEM SAFETY REST AREA
JANGTEOMOK SHELTER

109
00:05:29,203 --> 00:05:33,207
MODERATE DIFFICULTY

110
00:05:34,334 --> 00:05:36,210
FOR ABOUT 2 HOURS

111
00:05:36,294 --> 00:05:39,756
STONES, SNOW, LEAVES, ICE

112
00:05:40,631 --> 00:05:43,301
WHEN THE DIFFICULT SECTION ENDS

113
00:05:44,469 --> 00:05:46,304
FOR ABOUT 2 HOURS

114
00:05:46,387 --> 00:05:47,263
DIRT ROAD

115
00:05:47,346 --> 00:05:48,389
FLAT GROUND

116
00:05:48,473 --> 00:05:49,307
RUBBER MATS

117
00:05:49,390 --> 00:05:51,559
A GENTLE INCLINE

118
00:05:51,642 --> 00:05:54,312
A KIND AND FRIENDLY TRAIL
IS IN LINE FOR THEM

119
00:05:55,396 --> 00:05:59,942
JOY IS CERTAIN TO COME AFTER THE SUFFERING
ON THE BAEKMUDONG TRAIL

120
00:06:00,777 --> 00:06:03,071
ESTIMATED TO TAKE 4 HOURS
TO GET TO JANGTEOMOK SHELTER

121
00:06:04,947 --> 00:06:08,409
THE BAEKMUDONG TEAM STARTS HIKING

122
00:06:10,369 --> 00:06:13,331
THE BAEKMUDONG TEAM WALKS
WHILE BREATHING IN THE MORNING AIR

123
00:06:16,542 --> 00:06:19,712
THE TRAIL IS PRETTY EASY
UP UNTIL THE ENTRANCE

124
00:06:19,796 --> 00:06:21,172
HOWEVER

125
00:06:21,255 --> 00:06:24,592
THEY IMMEDIATELY ENTER
TO THE DIFFICULT PART

126
00:06:24,675 --> 00:06:26,969
THE STRUGGLE BEGINS

127
00:06:28,096 --> 00:06:31,099
A ROCKY PATH WITH NO SUNLIGHT
FROM THE BEGINNING

128
00:06:32,100 --> 00:06:33,059
EXHALING

129
00:06:33,142 --> 00:06:35,770
This must be
the difficult beginning of the trail.

130
00:06:35,853 --> 00:06:37,021
Looks like it.

131
00:06:37,105 --> 00:06:37,980
Right?

132
00:06:38,648 --> 00:06:39,816
This is…

133
00:06:41,275 --> 00:06:42,443
This isn't a mountain.

134
00:06:42,527 --> 00:06:44,821
Compared to all the suffering
they've put us through…

135
00:06:44,904 --> 00:06:45,738
Exactly.

136
00:06:46,739 --> 00:06:48,950
Jirisan is nice.

137
00:06:49,033 --> 00:06:50,576
Jirisan.

138
00:06:52,161 --> 00:06:56,165
THE EXCITEMENT OF THE LAST HIKE
MAKES THEM FORGET THE TRAIL'S DIFFICULTY

139
00:06:56,249 --> 00:06:57,542
What a nice mountain.

140
00:06:58,334 --> 00:06:59,210
PRAISING JIRISAN

141
00:06:59,293 --> 00:07:00,795
The air is so fresh.

142
00:07:00,878 --> 00:07:02,046
PRAISING JIRISAN AGAIN

143
00:07:04,841 --> 00:07:07,802
The streams sound so nice today.

144
00:07:07,885 --> 00:07:08,803
It's nice.

145
00:07:08,886 --> 00:07:09,720
Right?

146
00:07:09,804 --> 00:07:10,638
It's nice.

147
00:07:10,721 --> 00:07:12,598
EVEN THE WATER SOUNDS NICE

148
00:07:13,724 --> 00:07:14,851
Gosh, the phytoncides.

149
00:07:15,977 --> 00:07:17,270
I smell something.

150
00:07:17,353 --> 00:07:18,354
A MONTH AGO ON HALLASAN

151
00:07:18,438 --> 00:07:20,940
These cedars emit a lot of phytoncides.

152
00:07:21,023 --> 00:07:22,150
It just smells like trees.

153
00:07:26,154 --> 00:07:30,199
TODAY, HE MENTIONS THE PHYTONCIDES HIMSELF

154
00:07:30,283 --> 00:07:31,451
JIRISAN JUNGSANRI PARKING LOT

155
00:07:32,034 --> 00:07:34,203
SAN 112-1, SANCHEONG-GUN,
SOUTH GYEONGSANG PROVINCE

156
00:07:34,287 --> 00:07:36,289
CURRENT TIME

157
00:07:36,372 --> 00:07:38,458
THE JUNGSANRI TEAM IS PREPARING TO DEPART

158
00:07:39,208 --> 00:07:40,835
It's not too windy today, right?

159
00:07:40,918 --> 00:07:42,920
No, the wind is gentle today.

160
00:07:44,046 --> 00:07:45,214
WIND SPEED
GENTLE AT 1.5 M/S

161
00:07:45,298 --> 00:07:46,507
I'm just glad there's no wind.

162
00:07:47,341 --> 00:07:49,552
STRETCHING BEFORE DEPARTURE

163
00:07:49,635 --> 00:07:51,804
NEW GEAR
ANKLE BRACES

164
00:07:51,888 --> 00:07:53,556
I came in pretty determined today.

165
00:07:53,639 --> 00:07:55,391
-Like I brought these.
-Right.

166
00:07:55,475 --> 00:07:56,726
-These…
-What are they?

167
00:07:56,809 --> 00:07:58,603
When I used to work
at a construction site,

168
00:07:59,187 --> 00:08:01,898
I didn't want my clothes
to get caught on metal or anything.

169
00:08:01,981 --> 00:08:04,567
LIFE EXPERIENCES TAUGHT HIM
TO BRING ANKLE BRACES

170
00:08:04,650 --> 00:08:07,028
Your clothes became brighter,
and your socks are pink.

171
00:08:07,111 --> 00:08:08,446
I ordered the wrong socks.

172
00:08:08,529 --> 00:08:10,406
BABY PINK

173
00:08:10,490 --> 00:08:13,159
I brought my package unopened and as-is.

174
00:08:13,242 --> 00:08:14,911
I opened it, and these pink socks…

175
00:08:16,829 --> 00:08:17,663
They were inside.

176
00:08:17,747 --> 00:08:19,123
LUCKY PINK SOCKS FOR THE LAST HIKE

177
00:08:19,790 --> 00:08:21,375
What if you run into a bear today?

178
00:08:22,001 --> 00:08:23,753
Have you actually seen one before?

179
00:08:23,836 --> 00:08:25,630
I've never seen any in Korea.

180
00:08:25,713 --> 00:08:26,589
Really?

181
00:08:26,672 --> 00:08:28,716
Yes, and I've seen a few
in Japan and the US.

182
00:08:28,799 --> 00:08:30,134
Did you just stand still?

183
00:08:30,218 --> 00:08:31,302
Yes, you can't move.

184
00:08:31,385 --> 00:08:32,887
Didn't you say you only saw snakes?

185
00:08:32,970 --> 00:08:34,639
That was in Korea.

186
00:08:36,432 --> 00:08:37,433
Are you doubting him?

187
00:08:38,434 --> 00:08:39,644
Why would you doubt him?

188
00:08:41,312 --> 00:08:42,605
THEY START HIKING

189
00:08:42,688 --> 00:08:44,440
It's cold when you stand still.

190
00:08:44,524 --> 00:08:46,192
FILMING WAS DONE SAFELY

191
00:08:46,275 --> 00:08:47,568
UNDER THE GUIDANCE OF EXPERTS

192
00:08:48,110 --> 00:08:48,945
Here we go.

193
00:08:49,028 --> 00:08:50,613
-I hate this.
-Me too.

194
00:08:50,696 --> 00:08:52,323
GROANS

195
00:08:52,406 --> 00:08:55,284
THEIR STAGGERING HIKING TRAIL
THAT MAKES THEM GROAN TODAY

196
00:08:55,868 --> 00:08:58,329
THE JUNGSANRI TRAIL

197
00:08:59,038 --> 00:09:01,332
ANOTHER WELL-KNOWN JIRISAN TRAIL
IN THE YEONGNAM AREA

198
00:09:02,291 --> 00:09:04,335
IT HAS ITS UNIQUE LANDSCAPE

199
00:09:04,418 --> 00:09:07,296
CREATED BY ROCKS AND VALLEYS

200
00:09:08,130 --> 00:09:10,341
BUT IT REQUIRES MORE THAN AVERAGE STAMINA

201
00:09:10,424 --> 00:09:13,302
MODERATE SECTION
FOR 2 HOURS AND 30 MINUTES

202
00:09:14,845 --> 00:09:16,264
HELLISH INCLINES THAT NEVER END

203
00:09:16,347 --> 00:09:19,308
DIFFICULT SECTION
FOR 1 HOUR AND 20 MINUTES

204
00:09:22,311 --> 00:09:25,314
SUFFERING COMES AFTER SUFFERING
ON THIS TRAIL

205
00:09:26,440 --> 00:09:29,277
5.3 KM TO JANGTEOMOK SHELTER
TAKES ABOUT 4 HOURS

206
00:09:30,152 --> 00:09:31,404
It's cold at the start.

207
00:09:31,487 --> 00:09:33,948
CURRENT TEMPERATURE: -2.1°C
COLD FOR MARCH

208
00:09:34,031 --> 00:09:36,242
As I explained yesterday,

209
00:09:36,325 --> 00:09:38,953
this trail has moderate difficulty
in the beginning.

210
00:09:39,036 --> 00:09:41,247
But the last hour at the end is difficult.

211
00:09:41,330 --> 00:09:43,291
LEARNING ABOUT THE TRAIL AS THEY GO

212
00:09:43,374 --> 00:09:44,500
Did you come from far away?

213
00:09:44,584 --> 00:09:45,668
-Sorry?
-Come from far away?

214
00:09:45,751 --> 00:09:46,794
We're from Seoul.

215
00:09:46,877 --> 00:09:49,380
THE JUNGSANRI TEAM HAS A NEW MEMBER

216
00:09:49,463 --> 00:09:51,966
You could say
we represent hikers from Seoul.

217
00:09:52,049 --> 00:09:54,010
ARROGANT

218
00:09:54,093 --> 00:09:55,511
Have you been to Seoraksan before?

219
00:09:55,595 --> 00:09:56,554
Many times.

220
00:09:56,637 --> 00:09:58,014
Is that so?

221
00:09:58,097 --> 00:09:59,974
HE CAN FEEL THE VIBE OF A VETERAN

222
00:10:00,057 --> 00:10:02,560
I've been here more than 2,000 times.

223
00:10:02,643 --> 00:10:03,603
Two thousand times?

224
00:10:03,686 --> 00:10:05,438
Yes, for over 30 years.

225
00:10:05,521 --> 00:10:06,689
For over 30 years?

226
00:10:06,772 --> 00:10:08,566
THE NEW MEMBER
HAS AN INCREDIBLE TRACK RECORD

227
00:10:08,649 --> 00:10:09,900
You're a veteran.

228
00:10:10,651 --> 00:10:12,695
I'm a Seoul hiking expert, sir.

229
00:10:12,778 --> 00:10:14,488
-I see.
-Yes.

230
00:10:15,239 --> 00:10:18,075
If you have any questions about hiking,
you can ask me.

231
00:10:22,538 --> 00:10:24,248
He didn't answer me.

232
00:10:25,082 --> 00:10:26,208
He's not responding.

233
00:10:26,292 --> 00:10:28,002
BRAGGING TOO MUCH IN FRONT OF THE VETERAN

234
00:10:28,544 --> 00:10:30,588
I'll see how good you are as I follow you.

235
00:10:30,671 --> 00:10:31,505
Okay.

236
00:10:35,676 --> 00:10:38,262
AS HE FOLLOWS IN THE STEPS
OF THE SELF-PROCLAIMED EXPERT

237
00:10:38,929 --> 00:10:40,556
This is Jungsanri Valley.

238
00:10:42,099 --> 00:10:43,851
LOCATED NEXT TO THE TRAIL

239
00:10:47,980 --> 00:10:51,442
JUNGSANRI VALLEY

240
00:10:53,152 --> 00:10:55,613
<i>We'll go all the way up</i>
<i>along the Jungsanri Valley.</i>

241
00:10:55,696 --> 00:10:57,948
JUNGSANRI VALLEY WILL BE
THEIR HIKING COMPANION TODAY

242
00:10:58,949 --> 00:11:00,368
<i>There are other valleys in between.</i>

243
00:11:00,451 --> 00:11:01,577
BEOPCHEONGYEGOK VALLEY

244
00:11:02,161 --> 00:11:03,120
<i>A waterfall.</i>

245
00:11:03,204 --> 00:11:04,038
YUAMPOKPO FALLS

246
00:11:05,122 --> 00:11:05,998
<i>Ice walls.</i>

247
00:11:07,625 --> 00:11:10,961
<i>There's a lot of beautiful scenery,</i>
<i>which is Car-the's favorite.</i>

248
00:11:15,758 --> 00:11:18,636
I'm not wearing a beanie today,
so I hear him better. Darn.

249
00:11:18,719 --> 00:11:20,096
BICKERING WITH THE DOCENT TODAY

250
00:11:20,179 --> 00:11:21,514
I can't hear him with it on.

251
00:11:21,597 --> 00:11:23,099
5.1 KM TO JANGTEOMOK SHELTER

252
00:11:23,182 --> 00:11:24,558
THEY'VE ONLY WALKED 0.2 KM

253
00:11:25,768 --> 00:11:27,311
EXHALING

254
00:11:28,854 --> 00:11:30,815
BREATHING OUT

255
00:11:30,898 --> 00:11:33,734
UNLIKE HIS USUAL SELF,
CHAE-MIN IS BREATHING HEAVILY

256
00:11:37,738 --> 00:11:40,950
HE DOESN'T SEEM TO BE IN GOOD CONDITION

257
00:11:41,033 --> 00:11:42,576
Does he have a cold?

258
00:11:42,660 --> 00:11:43,911
Chae-min, do you have a cold?

259
00:11:44,995 --> 00:11:48,124
I had allergies act up yesterday.
I think I have a head cold now.

260
00:11:48,207 --> 00:11:50,126
<i>I took allergy medicine,</i>

261
00:11:50,209 --> 00:11:52,086
but at night, my nose…

262
00:11:53,212 --> 00:11:54,088
kept feeling strange.

263
00:11:54,171 --> 00:11:57,925
The next day,
I took the cold medicine I brought.

264
00:11:58,676 --> 00:12:00,678
LAST NIGHT

265
00:12:01,637 --> 00:12:04,306
HE TOOK HIS ALLERGY MEDICINE

266
00:12:05,057 --> 00:12:07,059
THIS MORNING

267
00:12:11,689 --> 00:12:14,608
HE EVEN TOOK COLD MEDICINE

268
00:12:14,692 --> 00:12:16,694
I had a few symptoms,

269
00:12:16,777 --> 00:12:20,573
but as soon as I was exposed
to the cold wind, it really hit me.

270
00:12:20,656 --> 00:12:21,824
THE ACE'S FIRST CRISIS

271
00:12:21,907 --> 00:12:23,075
This is bad.

272
00:12:24,952 --> 00:12:25,786
Let's go.

273
00:12:25,870 --> 00:12:26,704
LET'S GO HOME

274
00:12:26,787 --> 00:12:27,705
I'm okay.

275
00:12:27,788 --> 00:12:30,374
THE VIRTUE OF AN ACE IS TO NEVER GIVE UP

276
00:12:31,208 --> 00:12:34,128
CAN CHAE-MIN OVERCOME THIS HURDLE?

277
00:12:34,712 --> 00:12:38,340
MEANWHILE, THE BAEKMUDONG TEAM
IS IN GOOD CONDITION

278
00:12:38,424 --> 00:12:40,217
I don't hate mountains, after all.

279
00:12:40,968 --> 00:12:43,137
CURED HIS MOUNTAIN ALLERGY WITH POSITIVITY

280
00:12:43,220 --> 00:12:44,430
Jirisan is

281
00:12:45,681 --> 00:12:46,557
so green.

282
00:12:48,934 --> 00:12:49,852
Nice.

283
00:12:49,935 --> 00:12:50,895
The path is well-paved.

284
00:12:50,978 --> 00:12:53,814
THE POWER OF POSITIVITY MAKES
THE SNOW-COVERED MOUNTAIN LOOK GREEN

285
00:12:54,398 --> 00:12:56,275
This is Hadongbawi Rock.

286
00:12:56,817 --> 00:12:58,652
This is cool.

287
00:12:58,736 --> 00:12:59,695
Gosh.

288
00:13:01,113 --> 00:13:03,949
It's about 13 m tall
and about 15 m in circumference.

289
00:13:04,033 --> 00:13:05,409
That's insane.

290
00:13:05,493 --> 00:13:06,327
Right?

291
00:13:07,328 --> 00:13:09,747
TARZZAN VOLUNTARILY BECOMES
A DOCENT FOR THE FIRST TIME

292
00:13:10,706 --> 00:13:13,459
DOCENT TARZZAN'S FIRST EXPLANATION
HADONGBAWI ROCK

293
00:13:14,168 --> 00:13:15,628
Gosh, this is refreshing.

294
00:13:15,711 --> 00:13:17,671
CAN'T WAIT TO SEE
HOW POSITIVITY IMPACTS THE HIKE

295
00:13:17,755 --> 00:13:18,589
The weather's nice.

296
00:13:19,423 --> 00:13:22,051
WHAT WAS YOUR FIRST IMPRESSION
OF THE BAEKMUDONG TRAIL?

297
00:13:22,134 --> 00:13:23,385
It was really nice.

298
00:13:23,469 --> 00:13:26,514
It's true that I had
too much dopamine in me.

299
00:13:26,597 --> 00:13:28,682
Tarzzan and I hiked with smiles on.

300
00:13:28,766 --> 00:13:29,975
It was perfect.

301
00:13:30,059 --> 00:13:32,061
I thought, "Why am I so happy today?"

302
00:13:32,144 --> 00:13:33,979
I got so excited.

303
00:13:34,063 --> 00:13:36,440
It was finally coming to an end.

304
00:13:37,858 --> 00:13:39,818
"THE PROBLEM IS THE ATTITUDE,
NOT ALTITUDE"

305
00:13:39,902 --> 00:13:41,904
MOUNTAINEER ALBERT MUMMERY

306
00:13:42,446 --> 00:13:46,659
MEANWHILE, THE JUNGSANRI TEAM
HAS A LOT OF PROBLEMS

307
00:13:48,494 --> 00:13:49,453
There's a lot of rocks.

308
00:13:50,746 --> 00:13:52,623
SMALL ROCKS

309
00:13:53,207 --> 00:13:55,209
MEDIUM ROCKS

310
00:13:55,751 --> 00:13:57,503
BIG ROCKS

311
00:13:59,755 --> 00:14:01,840
IT'S ALSO SLIPPERY FROM THE RAIN AT DAWN

312
00:14:01,924 --> 00:14:04,843
THE PATH GOES ON WITH ROCK OF ALL SIZES

313
00:14:04,927 --> 00:14:07,137
<i>There were so many rocks today.</i>

314
00:14:07,221 --> 00:14:09,682
It felt like I was rock climbing
with my feet.

315
00:14:09,765 --> 00:14:13,060
Right up until you put your foot down,
you think, "Where do I step?"

316
00:14:17,106 --> 00:14:19,441
<i>My feet became very tense too.</i>

317
00:14:19,525 --> 00:14:22,236
I think this was
a very stressful mountain in many ways.

318
00:14:22,319 --> 00:14:23,779
CHAE-MIN FACED A LOT OF DIFFICULTIES

319
00:14:27,783 --> 00:14:30,160
THEY ARRIVE AT THIS LOCATION

320
00:14:30,244 --> 00:14:31,787
-Kalbawi Rock?
-It's Kalbawi.

321
00:14:33,831 --> 00:14:35,958
KALBAWI

322
00:14:37,126 --> 00:14:40,254
THE LANDMARK OF THE JUNGSANRI TRAIL

323
00:14:42,548 --> 00:14:44,592
THE ROCK'S TIP LOOKS LIKE A BLADE,
HENCE THE NAME

324
00:14:44,675 --> 00:14:47,428
This is the landmark
of the Jungsanri Trail.

325
00:14:48,095 --> 00:14:49,013
This is?

326
00:14:49,096 --> 00:14:51,140
YES, THIS

327
00:14:51,223 --> 00:14:52,558
Then, is that the small blade?

328
00:14:52,641 --> 00:14:55,060
BIG BLADE, SMALL BLADE

329
00:14:55,144 --> 00:14:56,020
You're right.

330
00:14:56,687 --> 00:14:57,563
INCREDULOUS

331
00:14:58,522 --> 00:14:59,565
His response just now

332
00:15:00,107 --> 00:15:01,025
was so annoying.

333
00:15:02,067 --> 00:15:02,902
YAWN

334
00:15:02,985 --> 00:15:05,738
This landmark marks
the beginning of the Jungsanri Trail.

335
00:15:05,821 --> 00:15:07,489
NOD

336
00:15:07,573 --> 00:15:10,659
We're 800 m above sea level here.

337
00:15:10,743 --> 00:15:11,744
KALBAWI

338
00:15:11,827 --> 00:15:13,495
MADE IT HALFWAY
TO JANGTEOMOK SHELTER

339
00:15:13,579 --> 00:15:15,414
As you can see, the incline…

340
00:15:15,497 --> 00:15:16,332
It's not too gentle.

341
00:15:16,415 --> 00:15:18,375
Yes, it's harder than moderate difficulty.

342
00:15:18,459 --> 00:15:20,628
STEEP FROM THE BEGINNING,
SO ALTITUDE RISES FAST

343
00:15:21,462 --> 00:15:24,423
AS THEY KEEP CLIMBING

344
00:15:25,716 --> 00:15:26,717
What's this?

345
00:15:28,260 --> 00:15:29,970
A SWINGING BRIDGE

346
00:15:30,054 --> 00:15:31,305
It was just a bit scary.

347
00:15:33,432 --> 00:15:34,433
Damn.

348
00:15:35,726 --> 00:15:39,605
ROCKS

349
00:15:40,189 --> 00:15:41,398
CHAE-MIN EXHALES

350
00:15:41,482 --> 00:15:42,650
There are many rocks.

351
00:15:43,734 --> 00:15:46,737
A SCREE TRAIL

352
00:15:47,613 --> 00:15:50,658
STAIRS

353
00:15:50,741 --> 00:15:52,534
This is Jungsanri Valley.

354
00:15:52,618 --> 00:15:54,328
The water is so clean.

355
00:15:54,912 --> 00:15:56,121
It's so clear.

356
00:15:56,205 --> 00:15:57,581
VALLEY

357
00:15:57,665 --> 00:15:59,083
Gosh, that startled me.

358
00:15:59,166 --> 00:16:00,000
What is it?

359
00:16:00,084 --> 00:16:01,210
I thought it was a fish.

360
00:16:01,293 --> 00:16:02,920
THEY'RE GOING THROUGH A VARIETY OF AREAS

361
00:16:04,922 --> 00:16:05,839
EXHALES

362
00:16:05,923 --> 00:16:08,717
THE ROCKS HAVE SCARY DROPS

363
00:16:08,801 --> 00:16:10,636
STAGGERING

364
00:16:11,345 --> 00:16:14,098
COULD TWIST YOUR ANKLES
ON THIS SCREE TRAIL

365
00:16:16,475 --> 00:16:19,353
THE STAIRS SLOW THEM DOWN

366
00:16:20,354 --> 00:16:24,108
AFTER ENDLESSLY GOING UP STEPS
AGAIN AND AGAIN

367
00:16:25,234 --> 00:16:26,860
This reminds me of Seoraksan.

368
00:16:26,944 --> 00:16:27,903
Yeah, it's similar.

369
00:16:27,987 --> 00:16:30,155
THEY'RE REMINDED OF SEORAKSAN

370
00:16:30,239 --> 00:16:35,327
It's how you need to use
your whole body to climb.

371
00:16:35,411 --> 00:16:36,328
Exactly.

372
00:16:36,412 --> 00:16:38,080
SEORAKSAN AND JIRISAN WERE SIMILAR?

373
00:16:38,664 --> 00:16:40,082
To put it simply,

374
00:16:40,791 --> 00:16:43,627
it felt like there wouldn't be
an easy section here either.

375
00:16:43,711 --> 00:16:46,005
You can feel it.

376
00:16:47,381 --> 00:16:49,925
THE BAD FEELING
THAT IT'S SIMILAR TO SEORAKSAN

377
00:16:50,551 --> 00:16:52,928
A FLAT GROUND
FOR THE FIRST TIME IN A WHILE

378
00:16:53,012 --> 00:16:54,555
Can I stop and have a chocolate bar?

379
00:16:55,097 --> 00:16:57,808
TIME FOR THEIR FIRST TRAIL FOOD

380
00:16:59,309 --> 00:17:02,021
TAKING A BITE RIGHT AWAY

381
00:17:03,689 --> 00:17:04,732
You can share this.

382
00:17:04,815 --> 00:17:06,859
HE DONATES TO THE PRODUCTION CREW TOO

383
00:17:07,651 --> 00:17:10,988
EVERYONE RECHARGES WITH CHOCOLATE BARS

384
00:17:11,572 --> 00:17:12,906
Are we a third of the way there?

385
00:17:12,990 --> 00:17:14,366
A third of the way to the shelter.

386
00:17:14,450 --> 00:17:17,161
THEY'RE ABOUT TO SET OFF AGAIN

387
00:17:17,244 --> 00:17:18,078
Hello.

388
00:17:18,162 --> 00:17:19,246
Good luck.

389
00:17:19,329 --> 00:17:20,914
Where are you all from?

390
00:17:20,998 --> 00:17:22,791
-We came from Seoul.
-Seoul?

391
00:17:22,875 --> 00:17:25,753
HE NATURALLY STARTS TALKING
NEXT TO CAR, THE GARDEN

392
00:17:25,836 --> 00:17:30,007
When we went up, a lot of seniors
talked to Car, the garden today.

393
00:17:30,591 --> 00:17:32,718
I think he gives off a friendly vibe.

394
00:17:33,719 --> 00:17:35,345
If you just look at his face…

395
00:17:36,180 --> 00:17:38,057
He might be hard to approach in the city.

396
00:17:38,140 --> 00:17:39,600
But when he's hiking,

397
00:17:40,601 --> 00:17:42,728
he clearly gives off the vibe

398
00:17:43,312 --> 00:17:44,855
that he lives in the mountains.

399
00:17:44,938 --> 00:17:46,398
PERFECT FACE TO TALK TO WHILE HIKING

400
00:17:46,482 --> 00:17:49,818
And he has a friendly smile.

401
00:17:49,902 --> 00:17:52,362
PROBABLY THIS KIND OF SMILE

402
00:17:52,446 --> 00:17:53,739
Your first time here? Or…

403
00:17:54,364 --> 00:17:56,325
-It's our first time at Jirisan.
-I see.

404
00:17:56,867 --> 00:18:00,537
If you go up there toward Cheonwangbong,
there's still snow. It's slippery.

405
00:18:00,621 --> 00:18:01,705
We brought crampons.

406
00:18:01,789 --> 00:18:03,165
Then, you're good.

407
00:18:04,625 --> 00:18:05,918
Have a nice day, sir.

408
00:18:06,627 --> 00:18:08,587
I'm not even 70 yet.
I'm not a grandpa.

409
00:18:08,670 --> 00:18:09,755
Hey, dude.

410
00:18:10,506 --> 00:18:12,091
Have a nice day, dude.

411
00:18:12,174 --> 00:18:13,509
I feel better.

412
00:18:13,592 --> 00:18:15,260
THEY RESUME HIKING

413
00:18:15,344 --> 00:18:17,930
THE CLIMBING SECTION STARTS AGAIN

414
00:18:23,811 --> 00:18:25,771
You can't help
but make a fuss as you go up.

415
00:18:26,522 --> 00:18:27,856
FROM CHAE-MIN'S CAM

416
00:18:27,940 --> 00:18:30,150
CLIMBING OVER BIG ROCKS

417
00:18:30,234 --> 00:18:34,113
<i>It felt like the rocks</i>
<i>were big and widespread.</i>

418
00:18:37,449 --> 00:18:38,283
Gosh.

419
00:18:38,367 --> 00:18:41,703
CHAE-MIN IS STRUGGLING MORE THAN USUAL

420
00:18:42,621 --> 00:18:43,789
I want to try going that way.

421
00:18:44,706 --> 00:18:46,959
PASSIONATE

422
00:18:47,626 --> 00:18:50,003
SKILLED

423
00:18:50,671 --> 00:18:52,673
PERFORMS A TRICK

424
00:18:53,382 --> 00:18:56,426
HE STAYS IN THE LEAD

425
00:18:57,553 --> 00:19:00,430
SHOWING HIS NEW SIDE

426
00:19:01,265 --> 00:19:03,142
Car-the is climbing really well today.

427
00:19:03,225 --> 00:19:05,561
THE EX-SPECIAL FORCES CAMERAMAN
ACKNOWLEDGES IT TOO

428
00:19:05,644 --> 00:19:07,729
I thought,
"He's hiking really well today."

429
00:19:07,813 --> 00:19:09,022
DESCEND CLUB'S ACE AGREES TOO

430
00:19:09,106 --> 00:19:11,316
And I happened to be not feeling well,

431
00:19:11,984 --> 00:19:13,277
so our paces matched up well.

432
00:19:13,944 --> 00:19:15,487
Car-the got faster

433
00:19:15,571 --> 00:19:16,780
and you got slower,

434
00:19:16,864 --> 00:19:18,198
so your speeds matched.

435
00:19:18,282 --> 00:19:19,241
THE PERFECT COMBO

436
00:19:19,324 --> 00:19:20,909
THEY WERE POLAR OPPOSITES

437
00:19:20,993 --> 00:19:22,744
We were polar opposites,
but we met halfway.

438
00:19:23,328 --> 00:19:26,331
SEORAKSAN

439
00:19:26,415 --> 00:19:27,457
This isn't right.

440
00:19:27,541 --> 00:19:29,626
HE COULDN'T EVEN CONTROL HIS OWN BODY

441
00:19:29,710 --> 00:19:31,670
-Go ahead.
-Okay.

442
00:19:31,753 --> 00:19:33,881
HE WAS BUSY GIVING UP THE LEAD

443
00:19:33,964 --> 00:19:36,216
TAEBAEKSAN

444
00:19:36,300 --> 00:19:37,759
It's really bad.

445
00:19:37,843 --> 00:19:39,636
-Really?
-It feels like they're tearing.

446
00:19:39,720 --> 00:19:42,598
GONE ARE THE DAYS
WHEN HE SUFFERED FROM A LACK OF SKILLS

447
00:19:44,850 --> 00:19:46,018
SOUNDING SURPRISED

448
00:19:47,144 --> 00:19:48,729
You're climbing so well.

449
00:19:49,479 --> 00:19:52,357
I have to go fast because it's scary here.

450
00:19:53,734 --> 00:19:55,944
CURRENT LOCATION
HOMBAWI ROCK SHELTER

451
00:19:56,028 --> 00:19:59,323
1 HOUR AND 50 MINUTES PASSED,
ARRIVAL AT HOMBAWI SAFETY SHELTER

452
00:20:00,991 --> 00:20:02,492
We took an hour and 50 minutes.

453
00:20:02,576 --> 00:20:04,661
TRAVELED DISTANCE: 3.0 KM,
REMAINING DISTANCE: 2.3 KM

454
00:20:04,745 --> 00:20:05,829
We've come a long way.

455
00:20:05,913 --> 00:20:08,040
A SHORT BREAK TO REGROUP

456
00:20:09,374 --> 00:20:12,085
FLUNG ONTO THE GROUND

457
00:20:12,920 --> 00:20:13,921
What on earth was that?

458
00:20:16,673 --> 00:20:17,549
Is it gone?

459
00:20:17,633 --> 00:20:18,800
I'll rescue it for you.

460
00:20:19,343 --> 00:20:21,011
-I'll get it back.
-My hands are weak.

461
00:20:21,094 --> 00:20:22,387
MAKING USE OF HIS GOOD CONDITION

462
00:20:22,930 --> 00:20:24,181
Gosh, Car-the.

463
00:20:25,933 --> 00:20:27,517
-Thank you.
-Let me stay here for a bit.

464
00:20:28,352 --> 00:20:29,353
It's comfortable here.

465
00:20:30,646 --> 00:20:33,106
A MERMAN FOUND ON JIRISAN

466
00:20:34,608 --> 00:20:35,734
Drop something else.

467
00:20:35,817 --> 00:20:38,237
SO I CAN LIE DOWN LONGER

468
00:20:39,488 --> 00:20:41,990
What on earth is happening?

469
00:20:42,074 --> 00:20:43,784
GRATEFUL BUT FLUSTERED

470
00:20:44,368 --> 00:20:45,535
We should put them on.

471
00:20:45,619 --> 00:20:47,162
THE BAEKMUDONG TEAM
ENTERS THE ICY AREA

472
00:20:47,246 --> 00:20:49,289
Should we put on crampons
and take five up there?

473
00:20:49,373 --> 00:20:50,749
Okay.

474
00:20:50,832 --> 00:20:51,667
All right.

475
00:20:51,750 --> 00:20:53,418
THEY KNOW THE RIGHT TIME TO WEAR CRAMPONS

476
00:20:54,127 --> 00:20:55,462
THEY NATURALLY SIT ON A ROCK

477
00:20:55,545 --> 00:20:56,672
Nice.

478
00:20:58,715 --> 00:21:01,802
THEY PUT ON CRAMPONS WITH EASE

479
00:21:03,011 --> 00:21:04,388
Nice!

480
00:21:05,305 --> 00:21:07,933
I get why corporate bosses
like to hike now.

481
00:21:08,517 --> 00:21:11,436
HE'S FIGURED OUT THE MINDS
OF CORPORATE BOSSES AFTER 5 HIKES

482
00:21:12,521 --> 00:21:14,022
1 HOUR HIKED,
CRAMPONS ON

483
00:21:14,106 --> 00:21:15,315
<i>It's doable with crampons.</i>

484
00:21:15,941 --> 00:21:18,527
It's been a while with crampons on,
so it feels weird.

485
00:21:22,698 --> 00:21:24,408
What on earth? Are these really stairs?

486
00:21:26,410 --> 00:21:30,414
APPEARING AS SOON AS THEY PUT ON
THE CRAMPONS

487
00:21:31,290 --> 00:21:34,334
A SNOWY PATH THAT HAS LOST
ITS FUNCTION AS STAIRS

488
00:21:35,419 --> 00:21:38,463
THE SLOPE'S GRADIENT EXCEEDS 27% AS WELL

489
00:21:38,547 --> 00:21:42,301
FROM TARZZAN'S CAM

490
00:21:43,010 --> 00:21:45,512
It sure is tough with all this snow.

491
00:21:45,595 --> 00:21:47,014
It makes your ankles bend.

492
00:21:48,140 --> 00:21:50,475
ANKLES HAVE TO BEND
AS MUCH AS THE AMOUNT OF SNOW

493
00:21:50,559 --> 00:21:53,437
Doesn't it feel like
the last bit of Seoraksan?

494
00:21:54,021 --> 00:21:55,647
CHUCKLING

495
00:21:55,731 --> 00:21:57,524
Well, it's doable.

496
00:21:57,607 --> 00:21:59,818
DIAGNOSIS
EXTREMELY POSITIVE ON HIKING

497
00:21:59,901 --> 00:22:02,154
I'd be in a good mood
even if we went to Seoraksan today.

498
00:22:04,072 --> 00:22:05,282
Okay, should we get going?

499
00:22:05,365 --> 00:22:06,366
One, two, three.

500
00:22:06,450 --> 00:22:07,951
Let's go!

501
00:22:08,035 --> 00:22:09,077
"Let's go!"

502
00:22:09,619 --> 00:22:11,204
This is the first time

503
00:22:11,913 --> 00:22:13,999
I've see some color
in your face while hiking.

504
00:22:14,082 --> 00:22:15,125
You take the lead.

505
00:22:15,208 --> 00:22:16,460
Make sure they film you a lot.

506
00:22:16,543 --> 00:22:17,377
I will.

507
00:22:18,086 --> 00:22:20,130
WILL KEEP CAMERAS
ON THE ROSY-CHEEKED DOWOON

508
00:22:20,213 --> 00:22:23,050
It looks like they just entered
the "Stairs from Hell."

509
00:22:23,675 --> 00:22:24,676
The "Stairs from Hell"?

510
00:22:26,219 --> 00:22:27,596
That could've been us.

511
00:22:27,679 --> 00:22:29,264
Seriously.

512
00:22:29,348 --> 00:22:31,600
COLOR DRAINS FROM HIS FACE
AT THE NEWS OF THE STAIRS

513
00:22:31,683 --> 00:22:32,517
LAUGHS

514
00:22:32,601 --> 00:22:33,435
CHUCKLES

515
00:22:33,518 --> 00:22:34,603
GIGGLING

516
00:22:34,686 --> 00:22:37,105
LAUGHING

517
00:22:37,189 --> 00:22:40,484
CAN'T STOP LAUGHING AT THE THOUGHT
OF HOW THE TABLES HAVE TURNED

518
00:22:41,068 --> 00:22:42,027
This hike is enjoyable.

519
00:22:42,110 --> 00:22:44,071
THE ENJOYABLE MODERATE SECTION BEGINS

520
00:22:45,072 --> 00:22:46,615
Hey, is this even a mountain?

521
00:22:46,698 --> 00:22:47,866
Geez.

522
00:22:47,949 --> 00:22:49,993
EVERYONE LAUGHS

523
00:22:50,077 --> 00:22:52,204
This is what I call hiking.

524
00:22:53,080 --> 00:22:53,997
Exactly this trail.

525
00:22:55,207 --> 00:22:58,001
I could go nonstop
if all paths were like this.

526
00:22:58,085 --> 00:23:00,212
Dowoon, I could even run.

527
00:23:00,295 --> 00:23:01,880
Yeah, I could even walk to Seoul.

528
00:23:01,963 --> 00:23:02,923
Right?

529
00:23:04,257 --> 00:23:06,635
THEY STILL HAVE STAMINA,
SO THEY PLAY "FINISH THE PROVERB"

530
00:23:06,718 --> 00:23:08,887
We'll do "Finish the Phrase."
The category is proverbs.

531
00:23:08,970 --> 00:23:10,430
-What?
-The category is proverbs.

532
00:23:10,514 --> 00:23:11,348
Okay.

533
00:23:11,431 --> 00:23:12,265
Two heads are…

534
00:23:13,100 --> 00:23:14,142
Are better

535
00:23:14,976 --> 00:23:15,811
than some.

536
00:23:17,145 --> 00:23:18,313
Every journey starts…

537
00:23:18,814 --> 00:23:20,273
Faster on a bicycle.

538
00:23:21,274 --> 00:23:23,235
Before you leap.

539
00:23:23,318 --> 00:23:24,611
That's "Look before you leap."

540
00:23:24,694 --> 00:23:25,946
Right, it's "look."

541
00:23:26,029 --> 00:23:26,947
It was "look."

542
00:23:27,030 --> 00:23:28,240
LOOKING AT THE WRONG ANSWER

543
00:23:28,323 --> 00:23:29,699
It's the quiet ones…

544
00:23:30,826 --> 00:23:32,160
You have to give treats.

545
00:23:34,287 --> 00:23:35,705
Don't shoot the…

546
00:23:36,581 --> 00:23:38,083
He said they got shot.

547
00:23:38,166 --> 00:23:39,626
You should call the police then.

548
00:23:41,711 --> 00:23:43,171
This tree looks amazing.

549
00:23:43,839 --> 00:23:45,966
WHILE WALKING LEISURELY,
HE FINDS A TREE TO TALK ABOUT

550
00:23:46,049 --> 00:23:47,134
This is cool.

551
00:23:48,426 --> 00:23:51,638
DOCENT TARZZAN'S SECOND EXPLANATION
KOREAN STEWARTIA MADE BY JIRISAN

552
00:23:51,721 --> 00:23:53,640
If you made a hoodie out of this…

553
00:23:53,723 --> 00:23:55,183
HE WANTS A HOODIE WITH THIS PATTERN

554
00:23:55,267 --> 00:23:56,893
It's nice.

555
00:23:56,977 --> 00:23:57,978
Shall we go now?

556
00:23:58,770 --> 00:24:00,313
Didn't that look really nice?

557
00:24:01,898 --> 00:24:04,901
1.5 KM TO JANGTEOMOK SHELTER

558
00:24:04,985 --> 00:24:06,736
They said we're going there.

559
00:24:07,445 --> 00:24:08,905
-Where?
-There.

560
00:24:08,989 --> 00:24:10,365
HE SEES THE SHELTER WAY OVER THERE

561
00:24:10,448 --> 00:24:12,033
So that's the shelter?

562
00:24:12,576 --> 00:24:14,452
Do you remember the name of the shelter?

563
00:24:14,536 --> 00:24:15,370
It was Jangteo…

564
00:24:16,621 --> 00:24:17,581
Jangteo Village.

565
00:24:17,664 --> 00:24:19,291
-Jangteomok Shelter.
-Jangteomok.

566
00:24:19,374 --> 00:24:20,584
SURPRISINGLY GETS IT RIGHT

567
00:24:20,667 --> 00:24:22,836
Guess why it's called "Jangteomok."

568
00:24:22,919 --> 00:24:25,297
They must've sold stuff there
like a <i>jangteo,</i> or market.

569
00:24:27,591 --> 00:24:29,843
They climbed up
the mountain to sell stuff?

570
00:24:29,926 --> 00:24:32,762
PEOPLE CLIMBED UP THE MOUNTAIN
TO SELL THINGS HERE

571
00:24:32,846 --> 00:24:36,516
THE HIGHEST SHELTER IN KOREA
AT 1,653 M ABOVE SEA LEVEL

572
00:24:36,600 --> 00:24:39,769
MARKETS HAVE BEEN OPEN HERE
SINCE THE THREE KINGDOM ERA

573
00:24:40,353 --> 00:24:43,481
IT WAS A PLACE WHERE PEOPLE CONNECTED

574
00:24:44,065 --> 00:24:45,400
They're incredible people.

575
00:24:46,067 --> 00:24:48,778
If they had been entrepreneurs
in present day,

576
00:24:49,404 --> 00:24:51,198
they would've destroyed
convenience stores.

577
00:24:51,281 --> 00:24:52,115
A NATION OF HIKERS

578
00:24:53,241 --> 00:24:54,534
-We're almost here.
-Yes.

579
00:24:55,076 --> 00:24:55,911
Goodness.

580
00:24:56,661 --> 00:24:57,996
We're here!

581
00:24:58,079 --> 00:24:59,080
Let's run.

582
00:25:02,417 --> 00:25:03,418
I want to rest.

583
00:25:04,085 --> 00:25:05,128
Resting is the best.

584
00:25:06,213 --> 00:25:09,257
THEY START RUNNING TO REST

585
00:25:10,550 --> 00:25:11,801
Gosh, you run really well.

586
00:25:12,427 --> 00:25:13,261
Geez!

587
00:25:14,221 --> 00:25:15,305
Damn.

588
00:25:15,388 --> 00:25:16,306
Dowoon, are you okay?

589
00:25:16,389 --> 00:25:17,349
How do you run so fast?

590
00:25:17,432 --> 00:25:18,308
Sorry?

591
00:25:18,391 --> 00:25:20,227
THE STAMINA OF A HIKING NATION DESCENDANT

592
00:25:20,977 --> 00:25:21,853
Let's go, Dowoon.

593
00:25:34,991 --> 00:25:37,577
3 HOURS AND 30 MINUTES PASSED
ARRIVAL AT JANGTEOMOK SHELTER

594
00:25:38,578 --> 00:25:41,456
ARRIVED 30 MINUTES EARLIER THAN EXPECTED

595
00:25:45,418 --> 00:25:46,294
We're mountaineers.

596
00:25:48,338 --> 00:25:50,924
We did come up quite a bit, didn't we?

597
00:25:51,007 --> 00:25:51,883
Gosh, we're high up.

598
00:25:51,967 --> 00:25:53,134
CHEONWANGBONG

599
00:25:53,218 --> 00:25:54,678
THE JUNGSANRI TEAM IS STILL GOING UP

600
00:25:54,761 --> 00:25:55,929
Doesn't it look endless?

601
00:25:56,012 --> 00:25:56,888
Yeah.

602
00:25:56,972 --> 00:25:58,265
It really feels like Seoraksan.

603
00:25:59,057 --> 00:26:00,183
This is no different.

604
00:26:01,184 --> 00:26:02,644
And it'll get harder.

605
00:26:02,727 --> 00:26:04,187
-What?
-It'll get harder.

606
00:26:04,729 --> 00:26:05,689
This is only the start?

607
00:26:05,772 --> 00:26:06,606
Yeah.

608
00:26:07,274 --> 00:26:10,277
THE REAL HIKE HASN'T EVEN BEGUN YET

609
00:26:10,360 --> 00:26:12,362
LOOKING AT THE REMAINING TRAIL

610
00:26:12,445 --> 00:26:13,905
It's basically the same difference.

611
00:26:14,572 --> 00:26:17,117
So far, the average gradient was 19.2%.

612
00:26:17,200 --> 00:26:19,077
-Okay.
-The remaining path is 31.8%.

613
00:26:19,619 --> 00:26:21,121
It's been at least 19% so far?

614
00:26:21,204 --> 00:26:22,914
THE REMAINING PATH IS 1.5 TIMES STEEPER

615
00:26:22,998 --> 00:26:23,832
But…

616
00:26:23,915 --> 00:26:25,959
To me, this doesn't feel
like moderate difficulty.

617
00:26:26,042 --> 00:26:27,669
-I think it's hard.
-This is much harder.

618
00:26:27,752 --> 00:26:29,254
-And that part seems very hard.
-Yes.

619
00:26:29,337 --> 00:26:30,588
Hard and very hard.

620
00:26:30,672 --> 00:26:32,340
THE START OF HARD DIFFICULTY

621
00:26:36,094 --> 00:26:37,762
THE GRADIENT JUMPS DRASTICALLY

622
00:26:39,514 --> 00:26:41,349
THE PATH THICKENS WITH SNOW

623
00:26:43,476 --> 00:26:44,978
IT'S ONLY BEEN JUST A PREVIEW SO FAR

624
00:26:45,061 --> 00:26:46,771
FROM NOW ON, IT'S THE TRUE JIRISAN

625
00:26:47,689 --> 00:26:48,565
Yes.

626
00:26:48,648 --> 00:26:50,525
LEAD: CAR, THE GARDEN

627
00:26:50,608 --> 00:26:53,987
TAIL: CHAE-MIN

628
00:26:54,070 --> 00:26:55,780
FROM CHAE-MIN'S CAM

629
00:26:55,864 --> 00:26:56,823
What's with this place?

630
00:26:57,615 --> 00:27:00,118
<i>If the Gwaneumsa trail is hard,</i>

631
00:27:00,201 --> 00:27:01,870
<i>then the Jungsanri Trail is very hard.</i>

632
00:27:01,953 --> 00:27:04,622
<i>That's what came up when I looked it up.</i>

633
00:27:05,248 --> 00:27:06,416
The expression they used was,

634
00:27:08,376 --> 00:27:10,712
"Think of it as walking up a wall."

635
00:27:10,795 --> 00:27:14,841
"Flat ground? What's that?"
That's what it said.

636
00:27:14,924 --> 00:27:15,884
FROM CHAE-MIN'S CAM

637
00:27:15,967 --> 00:27:19,721
<i>I definitely understood what they meant.</i>

638
00:27:21,264 --> 00:27:23,266
It isn't easy here.

639
00:27:24,726 --> 00:27:27,979
IT'S NO JOKE FROM THE START

640
00:27:30,148 --> 00:27:32,275
Hey, you should rest. Take it slow.

641
00:27:35,403 --> 00:27:37,739
THE TRACKING SHOT CAMERA OPERATOR STOPS

642
00:27:37,822 --> 00:27:41,534
IT'S HARD EVEN FOR THOSE WITH GOOD STAMINA

643
00:27:42,827 --> 00:27:45,330
AND THE ICY SECTION CONTINUES ON

644
00:27:46,581 --> 00:27:49,334
THEY PUT ON CRAMPONS

645
00:27:49,417 --> 00:27:52,337
AND START ON THE ICY ROAD

646
00:27:52,420 --> 00:27:53,296
GROANS

647
00:27:54,339 --> 00:27:56,257
What a tiresome road.

648
00:27:56,341 --> 00:27:58,635
TWICE THE AMOUNT OF SNOW
THAN THE PREVIOUS PATH

649
00:27:58,718 --> 00:28:01,179
CHAE-MIN HIKES WITH HIKING POLES

650
00:28:02,013 --> 00:28:03,640
TAP

651
00:28:03,723 --> 00:28:07,143
STRATEGY: USES HIS POLES
TO CHECK THE NEXT STEP TO TAKE

652
00:28:07,727 --> 00:28:10,230
CAR, THE GARDEN HIKES HANDS-FREE

653
00:28:10,313 --> 00:28:13,483
FROM CAR, THE GARDEN'S CAM

654
00:28:14,442 --> 00:28:17,445
STRATEGY: MAKES FULL USE
OF THE ENVIRONMENT AROUND HIM

655
00:28:18,488 --> 00:28:20,031
Gosh, this incline is crazy.

656
00:28:21,449 --> 00:28:22,325
Goodness.

657
00:28:25,078 --> 00:28:27,580
THEY WALK UP THE STEEP AND ICY STONE STEPS

658
00:28:27,664 --> 00:28:29,833
FROM CAR, THE GARDEN'S CAM

659
00:28:29,916 --> 00:28:32,293
THE TOP HAS FROZEN OVER COMPLETELY

660
00:28:33,503 --> 00:28:35,588
GOING DOWN ON ALL FOURS IMMEDIATELY

661
00:28:35,672 --> 00:28:36,840
What is this place?

662
00:28:36,923 --> 00:28:38,299
Good question.

663
00:28:38,383 --> 00:28:40,677
CAR, THE GARDEN REACHES FIRST

664
00:28:40,760 --> 00:28:42,470
FROM CHAE-MIN'S CAM

665
00:28:45,515 --> 00:28:46,808
Damn it. This won't do.

666
00:28:47,934 --> 00:28:50,520
GETS DOWN ON ALL FOURS TOO

667
00:28:50,603 --> 00:28:51,813
FROM CHAE-MIN'S CAM

668
00:28:51,896 --> 00:28:55,608
HE GETS THROUGH
THE ICE WALL-LIKE FROZEN PATH

669
00:28:57,193 --> 00:28:58,903
It's more frozen than last time, right?

670
00:28:58,987 --> 00:29:00,530
Yes, we didn't see paths like these.

671
00:29:00,613 --> 00:29:01,906
Yeah, it's harder than before.

672
00:29:01,990 --> 00:29:04,367
EVEN THE EXPERIENCED ARE FLUSTERED
BY THE HARDER SNOWY PATH

673
00:29:06,369 --> 00:29:10,707
CHAE-MIN FOLLOWS SLOWLY

674
00:29:11,541 --> 00:29:13,334
GROANS

675
00:29:13,418 --> 00:29:14,419
This is insane.

676
00:29:14,502 --> 00:29:16,087
GRIMACING BUT NOT STOPPING

677
00:29:19,966 --> 00:29:21,050
FROM CAR, THE GARDEN'S CAM

678
00:29:21,134 --> 00:29:23,928
REGARDLESS OF THE PATH, HE KEEPS WALKING

679
00:29:24,929 --> 00:29:28,224
THE PACEMAKER IS DILIGENT TODAY

680
00:29:28,308 --> 00:29:29,642
SIGHING

681
00:29:29,726 --> 00:29:30,602
I'm so tired.

682
00:29:30,685 --> 00:29:32,103
IT'S NOT EASY FOR HIM

683
00:29:32,812 --> 00:29:33,646
By the way,

684
00:29:34,481 --> 00:29:35,315
honestly…

685
00:29:36,274 --> 00:29:38,777
I think the number of hikers increased

686
00:29:38,860 --> 00:29:40,695
because they don't come
to places like this.

687
00:29:41,237 --> 00:29:43,698
I'm serious. We're wasting our efforts.

688
00:29:44,282 --> 00:29:45,658
We've only gone on trails

689
00:29:45,742 --> 00:29:47,619
that hiking enthusiasts never go on.

690
00:29:47,702 --> 00:29:49,329
THE TRAIL HAS BEEN EMPTY TODAY

691
00:29:49,412 --> 00:29:52,040
We're doing a service
by telling people not to come here.

692
00:29:53,708 --> 00:29:55,418
Everyone, please enjoy your hike.

693
00:29:56,252 --> 00:29:57,337
TO THE VIEWERS

694
00:29:57,420 --> 00:29:58,630
SUDDENLY THE HIKING AMBASSADOR

695
00:29:58,713 --> 00:29:59,631
Just enjoy it.

696
00:29:59,714 --> 00:30:02,759
If you can handle this, then enjoy it.

697
00:30:02,842 --> 00:30:04,385
But if you lack stamina like I do,

698
00:30:04,469 --> 00:30:05,929
don't ever come here.

699
00:30:06,012 --> 00:30:07,180
It's foolhardy.

700
00:30:08,181 --> 00:30:10,016
It's a waste of time. Life is short.

701
00:30:11,017 --> 00:30:12,977
Don't waste your time on nonsense.

702
00:30:13,770 --> 00:30:15,438
Spend your time on something meaningful.

703
00:30:16,272 --> 00:30:17,148
I mean it.

704
00:30:17,232 --> 00:30:18,566
Hike according to your abilities.

705
00:30:18,650 --> 00:30:20,193
Yes, within your abilities and means.

706
00:30:20,276 --> 00:30:21,361
"Within your means."

707
00:30:21,444 --> 00:30:23,738
FROM SOMEONE WHOSE MEANS
WEREN'T SUITABLE FOR JIRISAN

708
00:30:26,157 --> 00:30:27,575
Do we have around 300 m left?

709
00:30:27,659 --> 00:30:29,577
There's about 300 to 400 m left.

710
00:30:29,661 --> 00:30:32,080
-About 400 m?
-It's 10:07 a.m. right now.

711
00:30:32,163 --> 00:30:33,790
We planned to arrive by 10:30 a.m.

712
00:30:33,873 --> 00:30:36,292
-We should arrive close to that.
-Pretty much.

713
00:30:36,376 --> 00:30:38,962
Nice. We're still pretty fast.

714
00:30:39,045 --> 00:30:41,548
You did better than I thought today.

715
00:30:41,631 --> 00:30:44,008
THANKS TO THE PACEMAKER,
THEY'RE MAINTAINING THEIR SPEED

716
00:30:44,092 --> 00:30:46,261
The whole production crew is shocked.

717
00:30:46,344 --> 00:30:47,679
They must be disappointed in you.

718
00:30:47,762 --> 00:30:49,138
We're very disappointed.

719
00:30:49,222 --> 00:30:51,975
THE ONLY CELEBRITY
WHO IS DISAPPOINTING IF HE CLIMBS WELL

720
00:30:52,058 --> 00:30:55,270
<i>The production crew</i>
<i>was really disappointed.</i>

721
00:30:55,353 --> 00:30:56,229
Right.

722
00:30:56,312 --> 00:30:57,397
We thought you'd go slowly.

723
00:30:57,480 --> 00:30:59,732
I'm sorry to them.

724
00:30:59,816 --> 00:31:00,692
CAN'T TRUST HIM NOW

725
00:31:00,775 --> 00:31:02,610
They were flustered
because you had improved.

726
00:31:03,361 --> 00:31:05,405
The crew's more tired than you'd expect.

727
00:31:05,947 --> 00:31:08,825
THEY FOLLOW THE LEAD
OF THE IMPROVED CLIMBER GARDEN

728
00:31:09,534 --> 00:31:12,078
ABOUT 400 M LEFT

729
00:31:18,251 --> 00:31:20,253
I can't believe how steep it is here.

730
00:31:22,130 --> 00:31:26,384
THEY BARELY CAN TAKE A STEP PER SECOND

731
00:31:31,389 --> 00:31:33,391
FROM CAR, THE GARDEN'S CAM

732
00:31:34,017 --> 00:31:35,101
This is even harder.

733
00:31:37,437 --> 00:31:38,313
There's no end.

734
00:31:38,396 --> 00:31:41,149
THE PATH GETS STEEPER, LET ALONE END

735
00:31:42,275 --> 00:31:43,943
GROANS

736
00:31:44,027 --> 00:31:45,028
What's with this?

737
00:31:46,154 --> 00:31:49,407
THE BRUTAL AREA
WITH AVERAGE GRADIENT OF 31.8%

738
00:31:52,535 --> 00:31:55,622
HE CLIMBS ON ALL FOURS AGAIN

739
00:31:55,705 --> 00:31:58,458
FROM CAR, THE GARDEN'S CAM

740
00:31:58,541 --> 00:32:00,001
SIGHS

741
00:32:01,294 --> 00:32:04,005
THEY TRY TO PICK UP THE PACE

742
00:32:08,051 --> 00:32:11,429
THEY PAUSE AFTER LESS THAN TEN STEPS

743
00:32:12,013 --> 00:32:15,266
THEY CAN'T EVEN RAISE THEIR HEADS

744
00:32:15,350 --> 00:32:17,477
FROM CAR, THE GARDEN'S CAM

745
00:32:17,560 --> 00:32:19,854
HE PULLS HIMSELF TOGETHER

746
00:32:25,652 --> 00:32:28,029
PANTING

747
00:32:30,865 --> 00:32:33,451
IN THE END, HE STOPS AGAIN

748
00:32:34,035 --> 00:32:35,036
This is so tough.

749
00:32:43,753 --> 00:32:46,506
THEIR STAMINA RUNS OUT QUICKLY
DUE TO THE STEEP SLOPE

750
00:32:46,589 --> 00:32:48,174
You just need to go ten more minutes.

751
00:32:48,967 --> 00:32:50,760
Which was the hardest part?

752
00:32:52,178 --> 00:32:53,972
Right before the shelter.

753
00:32:54,055 --> 00:32:54,889
That spot?

754
00:32:55,598 --> 00:32:57,100
That section had no mercy.

755
00:32:57,183 --> 00:32:58,017
That place…

756
00:32:58,101 --> 00:33:00,561
SICK OF IT

757
00:33:00,645 --> 00:33:02,146
I mean, what do you want me to do?

758
00:33:02,230 --> 00:33:04,315
What do you want from me?

759
00:33:04,399 --> 00:33:07,402
It felt like the path said,
"Come if you want. If not, then don't."

760
00:33:08,611 --> 00:33:09,904
STRAINING

761
00:33:09,988 --> 00:33:11,531
NEGATIVE GARDEN IS GETTING MAD

762
00:33:11,614 --> 00:33:12,490
Where's the end?

763
00:33:14,367 --> 00:33:16,911
Why does Jangteomok Shelter
feel so high up?

764
00:33:16,995 --> 00:33:18,830
<i>Chae-min got a bit angry today too.</i>

765
00:33:19,998 --> 00:33:22,834
It's rare to see him do that.

766
00:33:24,252 --> 00:33:25,253
So, it really was hard.

767
00:33:27,964 --> 00:33:30,383
SAYS THE PERSON WHO'S THE MOST ANGRY

768
00:33:36,264 --> 00:33:38,975
GETTING MORE AND MORE WORKED UP

769
00:33:39,976 --> 00:33:41,436
****, look at that.

770
00:33:41,519 --> 00:33:45,148
RELEASING THE CURSES
HE'S BEEN HOLDING BACK

771
00:33:45,231 --> 00:33:47,483
TWO MONTHS AGO AT SEORAKSAN

772
00:33:47,567 --> 00:33:49,652
I couldn't hold myself back from cursing.

773
00:33:49,736 --> 00:33:50,611
I'm serious.

774
00:33:50,695 --> 00:33:52,405
You can curse if it's too hard.

775
00:33:53,281 --> 00:33:54,323
I can't hold it back.

776
00:33:54,407 --> 00:33:55,992
HIS TEACHER'S LESSONS ON SEORAKSAN

777
00:33:56,576 --> 00:33:57,869
THE MODEL STUDENT DOES AS TAUGHT

778
00:33:57,952 --> 00:33:58,786
F***.

779
00:33:58,870 --> 00:34:00,663
G********.

780
00:34:03,708 --> 00:34:06,627
MAKING FULL USE OF WHAT HE LEARNED

781
00:34:08,379 --> 00:34:09,213
This m************…

782
00:34:09,297 --> 00:34:11,340
USING HIS MOUTH AS A SPEED BOOST

783
00:34:11,424 --> 00:34:13,926
HE SQUEEZES OUT
THE LAST DROP OF ENERGY TO CLIMB

784
00:34:14,010 --> 00:34:15,178
It's our sound mixer!

785
00:34:15,261 --> 00:34:16,262
You can do it!

786
00:34:18,639 --> 00:34:19,974
-Who's that?
-They've arrived.

787
00:34:20,058 --> 00:34:21,976
THEY CAN FAINTLY HEAR THE BAEKMUDONG TEAM

788
00:34:22,894 --> 00:34:23,853
There they are.

789
00:34:24,771 --> 00:34:25,772
JUNGSANRI, BAEKMUDONG

790
00:34:25,855 --> 00:34:27,774
THE BAEKMUDONG TEAM IS WATCHING FROM ABOVE

791
00:34:27,857 --> 00:34:28,775
You can do it!

792
00:34:30,151 --> 00:34:31,194
You can do it!

793
00:34:31,277 --> 00:34:34,363
NO, I CAN'T

794
00:34:37,033 --> 00:34:40,328
IT'S REALLY RIGHT IN FRONT OF THEM

795
00:34:40,912 --> 00:34:43,039
CAR, THE GARDEN'S FACE
IS SEVERELY CONTORTED

796
00:34:43,956 --> 00:34:45,500
If we mess around too much…

797
00:34:45,583 --> 00:34:46,417
Jung-won!

798
00:34:46,501 --> 00:34:48,252
-If we mess around, he'll hit us.
-Really?

799
00:34:48,336 --> 00:34:49,212
DANGER DETECTED

800
00:34:49,962 --> 00:34:51,255
His expression looks terrible.

801
00:34:51,339 --> 00:34:52,215
SIGHING

802
00:34:52,965 --> 00:34:54,050
F***.

803
00:34:55,802 --> 00:34:58,930
Looking at how Chae-min in the back
doesn't look good either…

804
00:35:00,181 --> 00:35:01,766
Usually, he's smiling in the back.

805
00:35:06,479 --> 00:35:08,106
FROM CAR, THE GARDEN'S CAM

806
00:35:08,189 --> 00:35:09,482
Go ahead, Tae-min.

807
00:35:10,233 --> 00:35:11,651
Go on. Go ahead of me.

808
00:35:12,360 --> 00:35:14,237
TAE-MIN: NO, I'LL REST WITH YOU

809
00:35:15,113 --> 00:35:16,072
I feel like I'm dying.

810
00:35:18,407 --> 00:35:22,537
SQUEEZING OUT THE LAST DROP OF ENERGY
FOR THE HOMESTRETCH

811
00:35:23,663 --> 00:35:24,956
GOSH

812
00:35:26,124 --> 00:35:28,251
Gosh, we somehow made it.

813
00:35:29,252 --> 00:35:32,547
THE JUNGSANRI TEAM ARRIVES
AT JANGTEOMOK SHELTER

814
00:35:35,967 --> 00:35:37,009
It feels like Huiungak.

815
00:35:37,093 --> 00:35:38,386
Hey, don't talk to them.

816
00:35:39,929 --> 00:35:41,764
No joke. This place is…

817
00:35:41,848 --> 00:35:42,849
a ********.

818
00:35:42,932 --> 00:35:44,433
IT MAKES ME SAY NICE WORDS

819
00:35:44,517 --> 00:35:47,478
Forget about hiking.
It's a ********.

820
00:35:47,562 --> 00:35:48,646
A HEAVILY CONDENSED REVIEW

821
00:35:48,729 --> 00:35:49,564
Seriously.

822
00:35:50,231 --> 00:35:51,482
I have nothing else to say.

823
00:35:51,566 --> 00:35:53,025
HE'S STRANGE

824
00:35:53,109 --> 00:35:54,735
You swore a lot when you arrived.

825
00:35:54,819 --> 00:35:55,945
Yes.

826
00:35:56,028 --> 00:35:57,572
I can do it now too. Want to hear it?

827
00:35:58,739 --> 00:35:59,574
I want to

828
00:36:00,408 --> 00:36:01,534
tone it down.

829
00:36:02,285 --> 00:36:03,244
But it's ******* ****.

830
00:36:03,327 --> 00:36:04,745
IT WAS SUCH A HAPPY EXPERIENCE

831
00:36:04,829 --> 00:36:07,915
TREMBLING

832
00:36:07,999 --> 00:36:09,000
Seriously.

833
00:36:09,709 --> 00:36:12,420
Please bleep this out and air it.

834
00:36:12,503 --> 00:36:13,379
WE KEPT THE PROMISE

835
00:36:13,462 --> 00:36:14,380
Good job.

836
00:36:14,463 --> 00:36:15,298
Look at the sweat.

837
00:36:15,381 --> 00:36:17,884
JUNGSANRI TEAM ARRIVES
AT JANGTEOMOK SHELTER

838
00:36:18,593 --> 00:36:21,179
-I can't help it.
-Look at Chae-min…

839
00:36:21,971 --> 00:36:23,181
GLOWING

840
00:36:23,264 --> 00:36:26,309
I think I sweat out a liter.

841
00:36:26,893 --> 00:36:28,144
Frankly speaking…

842
00:36:28,769 --> 00:36:29,645
It's Seoraksan.

843
00:36:29,729 --> 00:36:31,814
Level-wise, it's harder than Seoraksan.

844
00:36:31,898 --> 00:36:34,609
I've never heard you say
something was hard.

845
00:36:34,692 --> 00:36:35,526
Seriously…

846
00:36:35,610 --> 00:36:37,361
NOT USED TO THE ACE BEING LIKE THIS

847
00:36:37,445 --> 00:36:39,614
I'm honestly glad
you guys didn't take our trail.

848
00:36:40,489 --> 00:36:41,449
The reason is

849
00:36:42,283 --> 00:36:43,326
if all four of us did,

850
00:36:44,243 --> 00:36:45,745
the atmosphere would've been hostile.

851
00:36:46,621 --> 00:36:48,998
THANK GOODNESS

852
00:36:49,081 --> 00:36:50,750
I'm glad the two of you had it easy.

853
00:36:51,459 --> 00:36:53,377
But your first half seemed tough too.

854
00:36:53,461 --> 00:36:55,379
YOU LOOK LIKE YOU HAD IT A LOT WORSE

855
00:36:55,463 --> 00:36:57,215
Wasn't it hard at first but easy later on?

856
00:36:57,298 --> 00:36:58,382
-Yes.
-That's what I heard.

857
00:36:58,466 --> 00:37:00,218
They didn't find
the first half hard either.

858
00:37:00,301 --> 00:37:03,930
TABLES HAVE TURNED FOR THE FORMER
SEONGPANAK AND GWANEUMSA TEAMS

859
00:37:04,472 --> 00:37:05,431
Shall we go eat?

860
00:37:05,514 --> 00:37:06,891
-Yes, let's eat.
-Let's eat.

861
00:37:06,974 --> 00:37:07,975
TIME TO EAT NOW

862
00:37:08,768 --> 00:37:11,312
JANGTEOMOK SHELTER KITCHEN

863
00:37:11,395 --> 00:37:12,897
I'm so hungry. Let's eat something.

864
00:37:12,980 --> 00:37:14,523
LUNCH MENU: RAMYEON

865
00:37:20,947 --> 00:37:23,950
CAR, THE GARDEN BROUGHT
CAMPING COOKWARE AND A PORTABLE GAS STOVE

866
00:37:24,784 --> 00:37:26,953
RUMMAGING

867
00:37:27,662 --> 00:37:29,956
THEY EACH BROUGHT THEIR OWN CUTLERY

868
00:37:33,125 --> 00:37:36,587
TARZZAN BROUGHT 4 PACKS OF RAMYEON

869
00:37:36,671 --> 00:37:37,755
DESCEND CLUB'S SELECTION

870
00:37:37,838 --> 00:37:38,965
SNACK RAMEN

871
00:37:39,048 --> 00:37:39,882
Let's buy <i>ramyeon.</i>

872
00:37:39,966 --> 00:37:41,384
LAST NIGHT, THEY BOUGHT RAMYEON

873
00:37:42,301 --> 00:37:43,302
What should we eat?

874
00:37:43,970 --> 00:37:46,180
This takes only two minutes.
Should we buy Snack Ramen?

875
00:37:46,264 --> 00:37:48,182
THE "2 MINUTES" CAUGHT
CHAE-MIN'S ATTENTION

876
00:37:48,266 --> 00:37:50,935
THEY CHOSE SNACK RAMEN,
WHICH CAN BE MADE FAST AND IS DELICIOUS

877
00:37:51,811 --> 00:37:53,938
2ND TIME COOKING IN A SHELTER
PREPARED FOR LUNCH WELL

878
00:37:54,021 --> 00:37:55,898
-This is enough.
-Just that much.

879
00:37:55,982 --> 00:37:56,941
ADD WATER FIRST

880
00:37:57,024 --> 00:37:58,442
I'll start the fire.

881
00:38:00,945 --> 00:38:01,904
It's working.

882
00:38:01,988 --> 00:38:03,864
LIGHT STOVE QUICKLY

883
00:38:03,948 --> 00:38:04,782
It'll be quick.

884
00:38:04,865 --> 00:38:07,243
THEY GATHER ROUND
AND WAIT FOR THE WATER TO BOIL

885
00:38:07,326 --> 00:38:09,287
It's starting to steam.

886
00:38:10,413 --> 00:38:12,039
SHAKING

887
00:38:13,124 --> 00:38:15,334
ADDS THE RAMYEON SOUP BASE FIRST

888
00:38:15,418 --> 00:38:17,628
Nice. You have to add
the soup base for <i>ramyeon</i> first.

889
00:38:17,712 --> 00:38:18,879
That's right.

890
00:38:19,880 --> 00:38:22,883
HE ADDS ALL 4 PACKS OF NOODLES AT ONCE

891
00:38:23,759 --> 00:38:26,053
DESCEND CLUB'S OFFICIAL RAMYEON COOKER,
CHAE-MIN

892
00:38:26,887 --> 00:38:28,848
-We need to cook it a bit more.
-A bit more?

893
00:38:29,974 --> 00:38:32,268
MEANWHILE, CAR, THE GARDEN PACES AROUND

894
00:38:32,351 --> 00:38:33,185
Aren't you tired?

895
00:38:33,269 --> 00:38:34,103
I am.

896
00:38:34,186 --> 00:38:35,229
Wasn't it so tiring?

897
00:38:35,313 --> 00:38:36,355
BADMOUTHING THE MOUNTAIN

898
00:38:36,439 --> 00:38:37,440
It's ridiculous.

899
00:38:39,275 --> 00:38:40,860
I hate that we have more left to climb.

900
00:38:41,986 --> 00:38:43,112
Am I looking too down today?

901
00:38:43,195 --> 00:38:45,239
SMILING GARDEN

902
00:38:45,323 --> 00:38:47,241
LONG-FACED GARDEN

903
00:38:47,325 --> 00:38:48,159
I'm depressed.

904
00:38:49,201 --> 00:38:52,663
I wish this was the end like Huiungak
and we could go back down.

905
00:38:52,747 --> 00:38:54,040
We thought that too.

906
00:38:54,582 --> 00:38:56,459
DESCEND CLUB NEVER CHANGES

907
00:38:57,501 --> 00:38:59,378
-It looks delicious.
-It looks good.

908
00:38:59,462 --> 00:39:02,757
I've been wanting to eat this
since the halfway point.

909
00:39:03,341 --> 00:39:05,176
I was like, "Two kilometers to <i>ramyeon."</i>

910
00:39:05,926 --> 00:39:07,720
It looks just nice and al dente.

911
00:39:07,803 --> 00:39:08,637
Yeah, let's eat.

912
00:39:11,390 --> 00:39:13,726
THE RAMYEON IS READY IN AN INSTANT

913
00:39:13,809 --> 00:39:14,977
Eat up.

914
00:39:15,061 --> 00:39:16,062
Okay.

915
00:39:16,896 --> 00:39:18,397
SCOOPING UP A BOWLFUL

916
00:39:26,947 --> 00:39:27,948
Gosh.

917
00:39:42,296 --> 00:39:44,465
This is the best <i>ramyeon</i>
I've had in recent memory.

918
00:39:44,548 --> 00:39:45,383
Me too.

919
00:39:50,262 --> 00:39:52,390
ONE BOWL CLEARED

920
00:39:56,811 --> 00:40:00,314
I really don't like <i>ramyeon</i> that much.

921
00:40:00,398 --> 00:40:01,899
But doesn't it taste good today?

922
00:40:01,982 --> 00:40:02,983
It's so delicious.

923
00:40:07,988 --> 00:40:12,827
HE SAID HE DIDN'T LIKE RAMYEON

924
00:40:18,582 --> 00:40:19,625
This is heaven.

925
00:40:20,418 --> 00:40:22,002
ECSTATIC

926
00:40:25,714 --> 00:40:27,508
POURING A CUP OF BROTH

927
00:40:30,010 --> 00:40:30,928
Try the soup.

928
00:40:31,011 --> 00:40:32,179
The soup is good.

929
00:40:32,263 --> 00:40:33,264
Bring it here.

930
00:40:34,014 --> 00:40:35,641
DISTRIBUTING SOUP

931
00:40:40,020 --> 00:40:42,481
NOT LEAVING A SINGLE DROP BEHIND

932
00:40:42,565 --> 00:40:44,191
Did you finish the soup?

933
00:40:44,275 --> 00:40:45,484
Yes, we finished the soup too.

934
00:40:46,485 --> 00:40:47,903
That was a good meal.

935
00:40:49,613 --> 00:40:51,490
TIDYING UP IN PERFECT UNISON

936
00:40:52,074 --> 00:40:54,368
WITH THE WET WIPES DOWOON BROUGHT

937
00:40:55,035 --> 00:40:56,996
WIPING

938
00:40:57,580 --> 00:40:59,331
A SIMPLE WIPE DOWN FOR THE COOKWARE

939
00:40:59,915 --> 00:41:01,667
ALL THE TRASH IS KEPT IN A BAG

940
00:41:02,293 --> 00:41:04,462
THE COOKING AREA CLEANLY WIPED DOWN

941
00:41:05,880 --> 00:41:09,008
THEY CLEAN UP PERFECTLY
TO END A PERFECT LUNCH

942
00:41:09,091 --> 00:41:12,845
TIME FOR THE LAST PART
OF CLIMBING TO CHEONWANGBONG

943
00:41:12,928 --> 00:41:15,556
It's 1.7 km to Cheonwangbong.

944
00:41:15,639 --> 00:41:17,016
It'll take an hour and a half.

945
00:41:17,099 --> 00:41:18,309
You can do it.

946
00:41:18,392 --> 00:41:19,852
EVERYONE IS SILENT

947
00:41:19,935 --> 00:41:25,858
DIFFICULTY LEVEL UNTIL CHEONWANGBONG
HARD

948
00:41:25,941 --> 00:41:28,152
CHEONWANGBONG

949
00:41:28,235 --> 00:41:31,155
REMAINING DISTANCE: 1.7 KM
ESTIMATED TO TAKE 1 HOUR AND 30 MINUTES

950
00:41:31,238 --> 00:41:34,408
THEY DEPART FOR CHEONWANGBONG

951
00:41:34,492 --> 00:41:36,994
DESCEND CLUB HIKES AT FULL STRENGTH

952
00:41:37,077 --> 00:41:38,329
It's cold.

953
00:41:38,412 --> 00:41:39,288
Yeah.

954
00:41:39,371 --> 00:41:41,207
-My body is getting stiff.
-Mine too.

955
00:41:42,249 --> 00:41:44,919
THEIR BODIES BECAME
COLDER AND STIFF WHILE RESTING

956
00:41:45,544 --> 00:41:46,587
LEAD: CAR, THE GARDEN

957
00:41:46,670 --> 00:41:47,880
MIDDLE 1: DOWOON

958
00:41:47,963 --> 00:41:49,340
MIDDLE 2: TARZZAN

959
00:41:49,423 --> 00:41:51,425
TAIL: CHAE-MIN

960
00:41:51,509 --> 00:41:55,012
MATCHING THE SPEED OF THE PACEMAKER

961
00:41:55,095 --> 00:41:59,308
STARTING WITH STONE STAIRS

962
00:41:59,975 --> 00:42:03,020
AS THEY CLIMB THE STONE STAIRS

963
00:42:03,103 --> 00:42:04,021
It's pretty cold.

964
00:42:06,148 --> 00:42:11,237
SNOW HASN'T MELTED IN SOME PLACES

965
00:42:11,320 --> 00:42:15,199
HANDRAILS SOON APPEAR

966
00:42:15,282 --> 00:42:20,371
WHEN THERE ARE HANDRAILS…

967
00:42:20,454 --> 00:42:26,418
IT MEANS IT'S SO DIFFICULT
YOU NEED TO HOLD ONTO HANDRAILS

968
00:42:28,462 --> 00:42:31,465
CHAE-MIN QUICKLY RUNS OUT OF BREATH

969
00:42:33,008 --> 00:42:36,053
SIGHING

970
00:42:36,136 --> 00:42:37,429
What's easy about this?

971
00:42:38,013 --> 00:42:39,890
It's only difficult here at the beginning.

972
00:42:39,974 --> 00:42:41,475
-Here?
-Yes.

973
00:42:45,437 --> 00:42:46,939
EXHALING

974
00:42:47,022 --> 00:42:50,234
HE STILL FEELS UNWELL

975
00:42:50,317 --> 00:42:51,735
After you leave the shelter,

976
00:42:52,570 --> 00:42:56,240
the first part of the hike
feels tough again psychologically.

977
00:42:56,323 --> 00:42:57,324
And physically too.

978
00:42:59,201 --> 00:43:01,662
You take a long rest, eat something warm,

979
00:43:02,204 --> 00:43:05,416
sit down and so on,
and that makes your body relax.

980
00:43:05,499 --> 00:43:07,459
So, it feels you lose motivation.

981
00:43:08,335 --> 00:43:09,878
<i>And you lose energy too.</i>

982
00:43:09,962 --> 00:43:12,881
<i>My muscles go,</i>
<i>"Are we resting now?" and relax.</i>

983
00:43:14,466 --> 00:43:17,886
It feels like your body is telling you,
"You can't go."

984
00:43:18,512 --> 00:43:19,972
That was the best we could've done.

985
00:43:20,055 --> 00:43:22,182
We should've stopped there and descended.

986
00:43:23,475 --> 00:43:25,269
Like how we did on Seoraksan.

987
00:43:25,352 --> 00:43:26,604
Just to the shelter?

988
00:43:26,687 --> 00:43:28,772
After eating,

989
00:43:29,648 --> 00:43:31,692
I must've become a bit bloated.

990
00:43:31,775 --> 00:43:32,901
It was so tough.

991
00:43:32,985 --> 00:43:34,361
YAWN

992
00:43:35,946 --> 00:43:37,615
BASHFUL

993
00:43:40,367 --> 00:43:41,535
Damn it.

994
00:43:41,619 --> 00:43:42,911
SIGHING

995
00:43:42,995 --> 00:43:45,831
THE JUNGSANRI TEAM IS STILL SUFFERING

996
00:43:46,373 --> 00:43:48,834
PAUSES

997
00:43:49,960 --> 00:43:54,131
THE BAEKMUDONG TEAM HAD STAMINA LEFT
BUT IS NOW TIRED TOO

998
00:43:55,507 --> 00:43:57,134
GROANS

999
00:43:58,677 --> 00:44:00,095
My thighs are cramping like hell.

1000
00:44:08,270 --> 00:44:13,025
THEY END UP TAKING A BREAK
AFTER ONLY 5 MINUTES OF HIKING

1001
00:44:13,108 --> 00:44:14,985
My body got stiff

1002
00:44:15,944 --> 00:44:16,945
after eating <i>ramyeon.</i>

1003
00:44:17,696 --> 00:44:20,199
DAZED

1004
00:44:20,282 --> 00:44:21,992
Did you have a lot of this on your trail?

1005
00:44:23,327 --> 00:44:24,244
-Us?
-Yeah.

1006
00:44:24,328 --> 00:44:25,162
No.

1007
00:44:27,247 --> 00:44:28,874
We've had nothing but this.

1008
00:44:29,833 --> 00:44:31,293
I'm not joking.

1009
00:44:32,753 --> 00:44:33,587
Really.

1010
00:44:34,129 --> 00:44:35,464
You know when you get really mad?

1011
00:44:36,465 --> 00:44:37,758
It was like this the whole time.

1012
00:44:37,841 --> 00:44:38,884
THE PINEAPPLE HEAD IS MAD

1013
00:44:38,967 --> 00:44:39,802
Right?

1014
00:44:39,885 --> 00:44:42,930
Some places made me go,
"What am I supposed to even grab onto?"

1015
00:44:43,013 --> 00:44:47,017
<i>We suddenly went</i>
<i>from the Baekmudong trail to that one.</i>

1016
00:44:47,768 --> 00:44:50,771
The other side's trail was more…

1017
00:44:50,854 --> 00:44:52,648
Not other side. I mean…

1018
00:44:52,731 --> 00:44:54,441
Jung-won's trail.

1019
00:44:55,150 --> 00:45:00,197
I thought, "They went through
three and a half hours of this?"

1020
00:45:00,280 --> 00:45:02,241
We really had it easy.

1021
00:45:02,324 --> 00:45:05,577
Ours was like an easy version of Jirisan.

1022
00:45:06,328 --> 00:45:08,497
But you guys deserve
taking the easy trail too.

1023
00:45:09,206 --> 00:45:11,208
The bad thing is
my thighs are giving me the sign.

1024
00:45:11,917 --> 00:45:14,670
You are going really fast though.

1025
00:45:14,753 --> 00:45:15,754
I'll go at this speed.

1026
00:45:16,880 --> 00:45:18,424
I'm just worried it'll be hard on you.

1027
00:45:18,507 --> 00:45:19,758
Exactly. I'm beat.

1028
00:45:20,342 --> 00:45:22,803
I tried everything while going up.

1029
00:45:23,387 --> 00:45:24,805
I tried to go very slow.

1030
00:45:26,640 --> 00:45:28,600
But going very slow is excruciating too.

1031
00:45:28,684 --> 00:45:29,977
You think, "When will I arrive?"

1032
00:45:30,060 --> 00:45:31,145
Exactly.

1033
00:45:31,228 --> 00:45:32,229
You get that feeling.

1034
00:45:34,064 --> 00:45:38,986
"IF YOU'RE GOING THROUGH HELL, KEEP GOING"

1035
00:45:39,069 --> 00:45:43,949
"THAT IS NO PLACE TO STOP"
-WINSTON CHURCHILL

1036
00:45:49,413 --> 00:45:51,832
It's frozen here, so be careful.
It's completely frozen.

1037
00:45:51,915 --> 00:45:53,208
ENTERING A PARTIALLY FROZEN AREA

1038
00:45:55,210 --> 00:45:57,588
SLIPS

1039
00:45:57,671 --> 00:45:59,381
Didn't he just tell us to be careful?

1040
00:46:00,632 --> 00:46:04,678
YOU MUST BE CAREFUL
IF YOU'RE NOT WEARING CRAMPONS

1041
00:46:06,263 --> 00:46:07,848
You can do it, Jung-won.

1042
00:46:07,931 --> 00:46:08,974
You can do it.

1043
00:46:10,267 --> 00:46:11,143
What is this place?

1044
00:46:19,443 --> 00:46:20,402
It's slippery.

1045
00:46:21,278 --> 00:46:25,282
OTHERS PASS SAFELY

1046
00:46:28,118 --> 00:46:29,286
How am I supposed to go?

1047
00:46:29,369 --> 00:46:32,623
FROM CHAE-MIN'S CAM

1048
00:46:33,332 --> 00:46:35,542
TARZZAN WAITS FOR CHAE-MIN

1049
00:46:36,168 --> 00:46:41,131
CHAE-MIN TAKES A STEP WITH DIFFICULTY

1050
00:46:41,798 --> 00:46:42,633
Slippery, right?

1051
00:46:42,716 --> 00:46:44,384
Yeah, I should put on crampons.

1052
00:46:44,468 --> 00:46:48,013
I almost slipped
because I didn't have crampons on.

1053
00:46:51,433 --> 00:46:54,019
JUST LOOKING AT HIS FACE MAKES HIM LAUGH

1054
00:46:56,355 --> 00:46:57,231
Goodness.

1055
00:46:57,314 --> 00:46:59,858
NOW, THE RIDGE IS FREE OF ICE

1056
00:47:01,068 --> 00:47:02,861
We've come up so high already.

1057
00:47:04,154 --> 00:47:07,908
LOOKING AROUND

1058
00:47:07,991 --> 00:47:09,785
I don't see any higher mountain.

1059
00:47:10,619 --> 00:47:11,995
How much higher do we need to go?

1060
00:47:12,621 --> 00:47:14,748
FULL OF CONCERN

1061
00:47:15,624 --> 00:47:19,127
Do you remember the trees they use
for Christmas trees?

1062
00:47:19,211 --> 00:47:20,254
Yes.

1063
00:47:20,337 --> 00:47:21,713
Yew trees?

1064
00:47:21,797 --> 00:47:22,756
WRONG!

1065
00:47:22,839 --> 00:47:23,674
Korean fir trees.

1066
00:47:25,926 --> 00:47:27,594
HERE COMES THE EXPLANATION

1067
00:47:27,678 --> 00:47:29,680
This is a colony of Korean fir.

1068
00:47:29,763 --> 00:47:31,098
They're used for Christmas trees.

1069
00:47:31,181 --> 00:47:33,016
A COLONY OF FIRS
ON HALLASAN'S GWANEUMSA TRAIL

1070
00:47:33,100 --> 00:47:33,934
It's beautiful.

1071
00:47:34,560 --> 00:47:35,394
HALLASAN

1072
00:47:35,477 --> 00:47:36,311
KOREAN FIR TREES

1073
00:47:36,395 --> 00:47:37,813
EVERGREEN CONIFERS NATIVE TO KOREA

1074
00:47:37,896 --> 00:47:40,357
THAT GROW WILD AT ELEVATIONS
AT LEAST 1,000 M ABOVE SEA LEVEL

1075
00:47:40,440 --> 00:47:42,192
AND HAVE SPREAD OVERSEAS
AS CHRISTMAS TREES

1076
00:47:42,276 --> 00:47:47,447
JIRISAN

1077
00:47:48,949 --> 00:47:52,619
They're restoring Korean firs here.
That's why this place is meaningful.

1078
00:47:52,703 --> 00:47:55,497
ON THE VERGE OF GOING EXTINCT
DUE TO CLIMATE CHANGE

1079
00:47:56,623 --> 00:47:57,666
It feels like Jeju Island.

1080
00:47:59,918 --> 00:48:05,007
KOREAN FIR COLONY AT JESEOKBONG PEAK

1081
00:48:07,426 --> 00:48:08,260
I feel sleepy.

1082
00:48:09,386 --> 00:48:10,387
Me too.

1083
00:48:11,930 --> 00:48:14,391
Let's stay on the summit
for five minutes and go down.

1084
00:48:15,976 --> 00:48:17,269
Let's go down quickly.

1085
00:48:18,437 --> 00:48:21,565
A RESOLUTION BEFITTING OF DESCEND CLUB

1086
00:48:21,648 --> 00:48:22,691
Isn't this the peak?

1087
00:48:25,444 --> 00:48:27,279
I wish it was.

1088
00:48:28,113 --> 00:48:31,033
THIS PLACE WITH OPEN VIEWS ISN'T THE TOP

1089
00:48:31,116 --> 00:48:34,870
JESEOKBONG SHELTER

1090
00:48:34,953 --> 00:48:36,038
CURRENT LOCATION

1091
00:48:36,121 --> 00:48:38,665
1.1 KM TO CHEONWANGBONG

1092
00:48:38,749 --> 00:48:40,459
It's not that, is it?

1093
00:48:41,293 --> 00:48:42,169
It's not that, right?

1094
00:48:43,295 --> 00:48:44,504
-It is.
-What?

1095
00:48:44,588 --> 00:48:45,631
What?

1096
00:48:45,714 --> 00:48:46,632
-It's that?
-Where?

1097
00:48:46,715 --> 00:48:47,716
That is Cheonwangbong.

1098
00:48:48,258 --> 00:48:50,052
CURRENT LOCATION

1099
00:48:50,135 --> 00:48:52,721
THAT IS CHEONWANGBONG

1100
00:48:53,472 --> 00:48:54,431
Where?

1101
00:48:55,891 --> 00:48:56,975
That one in the distance?

1102
00:48:57,726 --> 00:48:58,602
What?

1103
00:48:59,144 --> 00:49:01,229
COLLECTIVELY DISAPPOINTED

1104
00:49:01,313 --> 00:49:02,356
Where's Cheonwangbong?

1105
00:49:02,439 --> 00:49:04,650
The peak in front of you.

1106
00:49:04,733 --> 00:49:06,360
It looks very steep.

1107
00:49:06,443 --> 00:49:07,694
CHEONWANGBONG

1108
00:49:07,778 --> 00:49:09,071
We shouldn't have come here.

1109
00:49:09,154 --> 00:49:12,658
Where we are now looks cool enough.

1110
00:49:12,741 --> 00:49:14,910
I'M (A PINEAPPLE) FINE

1111
00:49:14,993 --> 00:49:16,536
Yeah, it's the last hike.

1112
00:49:16,620 --> 00:49:19,289
We've gone 700 m, so there's 1 km left.

1113
00:49:19,373 --> 00:49:20,791
You felt it on Hallasan, right?

1114
00:49:20,874 --> 00:49:22,334
It's better when you can see it.

1115
00:49:23,335 --> 00:49:24,753
It gives you false hope.

1116
00:49:26,338 --> 00:49:27,673
I shouldn't say that.

1117
00:49:29,925 --> 00:49:31,218
But it is false hope.

1118
00:49:31,301 --> 00:49:33,387
NEUTRAL GARDEN FLIPS
BETWEEN POSITIVE AND NEGATIVE

1119
00:49:33,470 --> 00:49:34,304
Car-the.

1120
00:49:36,098 --> 00:49:37,849
<i>But that's life.</i>

1121
00:49:37,933 --> 00:49:43,146
It's fine when you can
more or less see what's coming.

1122
00:49:43,230 --> 00:49:46,108
But when you can't, you feel helpless.

1123
00:49:46,191 --> 00:49:49,194
I could see Cheonwangbong,
just like the peak on Hallasan.

1124
00:49:50,153 --> 00:49:50,987
So, it was okay.

1125
00:49:53,198 --> 00:49:56,868
<i>Jung-won said</i>
<i>that seeing it gave him hope.</i>

1126
00:49:56,952 --> 00:49:58,995
But I thought, "How do we get there?"

1127
00:49:59,079 --> 00:50:00,706
That was all I could think about.

1128
00:50:00,789 --> 00:50:02,207
Because it seemed so far.

1129
00:50:04,918 --> 00:50:06,086
Is that called perspective?

1130
00:50:06,920 --> 00:50:09,005
THE FLUSTERED PRODUCERS LAUGH

1131
00:50:09,089 --> 00:50:11,675
I don't think it has anything
to do with perspective.

1132
00:50:12,384 --> 00:50:17,931
CHEONWANGBONG LOOKS FAR AWAY
BECAUSE OF PERSPECTIVE

1133
00:50:18,724 --> 00:50:20,642
I'm so happy to go downhill.

1134
00:50:20,726 --> 00:50:21,601
I know.

1135
00:50:21,685 --> 00:50:25,105
IT'S DOWNHILL FOR ABOUT 300 M

1136
00:50:25,731 --> 00:50:30,235
THE HIKING BLUE CHIP
TAKES THE STAIRS FOR HIMSELF

1137
00:50:37,951 --> 00:50:39,286
Be careful here.

1138
00:50:41,246 --> 00:50:45,500
NIMBLE

1139
00:50:45,584 --> 00:50:48,628
HIKING SAFELY WITH HIKING POLES

1140
00:50:48,712 --> 00:50:53,675
A FORK IN THE ROAD APPEARS

1141
00:50:53,759 --> 00:50:56,553
CAR-THE GOES TO LEFT
DOWOON GOES TO RIGHT

1142
00:50:56,636 --> 00:50:59,055
TARZZAN FOLLOWS DOWOON,
HIS BAEKMUDONG PARTNER

1143
00:50:59,139 --> 00:51:00,557
Why are there different paths?

1144
00:51:01,141 --> 00:51:02,684
I'll go this way.

1145
00:51:02,768 --> 00:51:06,813
DOWOON ARRIVES FIRST

1146
00:51:06,897 --> 00:51:08,607
I followed you.

1147
00:51:09,149 --> 00:51:11,651
HE ARRIVES FIRST
BUT LETS CAR-THE TAKE THE LEAD

1148
00:51:11,735 --> 00:51:13,361
I should follow you now.

1149
00:51:13,445 --> 00:51:15,071
I choose easier paths, don't I?

1150
00:51:15,614 --> 00:51:16,740
You're a trailblazer.

1151
00:51:16,823 --> 00:51:17,657
Of course, I am.

1152
00:51:17,741 --> 00:51:19,451
TEAM BAEKMUDONG SHARES A DEEP BOND

1153
00:51:21,369 --> 00:51:22,954
Bam. Boldly and quickly.

1154
00:51:23,038 --> 00:51:24,664
And swiftly.

1155
00:51:25,749 --> 00:51:27,959
CHA JUNG-WON SHOWS OFF
HIS HIKING WITH IMPROVED SKILLS

1156
00:51:28,043 --> 00:51:29,211
Just like this. Boom.

1157
00:51:29,294 --> 00:51:31,296
Boom. And you step on just the rocks.

1158
00:51:32,339 --> 00:51:33,173
That's a tip.

1159
00:51:34,341 --> 00:51:37,135
HE VISUALIZES

1160
00:51:37,219 --> 00:51:38,261
AND PUTS IT TO PRACTICE

1161
00:51:38,345 --> 00:51:39,387
Boom.

1162
00:51:39,471 --> 00:51:40,722
Boom. Like this.

1163
00:51:40,806 --> 00:51:41,640
It's a three-step.

1164
00:51:42,933 --> 00:51:45,519
I'm bored today,
so I'm going to talk to myself on camera.

1165
00:51:48,188 --> 00:51:51,399
THE DOWNHILL SECTION ENDS

1166
00:51:51,983 --> 00:51:55,570
THEY PASS THE FLAT AREA

1167
00:51:55,654 --> 00:51:58,281
700 M TO CHEONWANGBONG

1168
00:51:58,365 --> 00:52:01,535
THE SNOWY UPHILL PATH BEGINS

1169
00:52:03,370 --> 00:52:04,621
This is a snow field.

1170
00:52:06,665 --> 00:52:10,669
STILL COMPLETELY COVERED IN WHITE SNOW

1171
00:52:11,253 --> 00:52:13,839
PANTING

1172
00:52:13,922 --> 00:52:15,799
ALTHOUGH TIRED,
CHAE-MIN TRIES TO STAY STRONG

1173
00:52:15,882 --> 00:52:16,716
Okay.

1174
00:52:17,676 --> 00:52:18,635
I can do it.

1175
00:52:19,553 --> 00:52:21,388
STARING

1176
00:52:22,097 --> 00:52:23,265
We're really almost there.

1177
00:52:23,974 --> 00:52:26,226
CHEONWANGBONG

1178
00:52:26,810 --> 00:52:28,478
-It's right in front of us.
-I can see it.

1179
00:52:28,562 --> 00:52:30,981
You're dead meat.
We're going to conquer you.

1180
00:52:31,982 --> 00:52:33,024
Can I use my speed boost?

1181
00:52:33,108 --> 00:52:33,942
Yes.

1182
00:52:36,403 --> 00:52:38,572
ATTACKED UNEXPECTEDLY

1183
00:52:39,155 --> 00:52:40,365
I'm sorry. It's uphill here.

1184
00:52:40,448 --> 00:52:41,783
I needed some momentum.

1185
00:52:41,867 --> 00:52:43,910
I thought you meant you'd go fast.

1186
00:52:43,994 --> 00:52:45,704
FLUSTERED BY THE UNEXPECTED CHEMICAL GAS

1187
00:52:46,538 --> 00:52:48,123
I needed some momentum.

1188
00:52:49,165 --> 00:52:51,668
TURNS OUT TO BE LAUGHING GAS

1189
00:52:51,751 --> 00:52:53,169
A SUSPICIOUS-LOOKING CAVE APPEARS

1190
00:52:53,253 --> 00:52:54,087
Goodness.

1191
00:52:54,170 --> 00:52:57,257
In front of you is Tongcheonmun,
which means "A gate to the sky."

1192
00:52:57,340 --> 00:52:58,925
THE NAME MEANS "A GATE TO THE SKY"

1193
00:52:59,009 --> 00:52:59,968
A GATE FORMED BY ROCKS

1194
00:53:00,051 --> 00:53:02,637
MUST WALK STRAIGHT UP THROUGH THE ROCKS

1195
00:53:02,721 --> 00:53:09,311
IT'S NARROWER AND STEEPER
THAN IT LOOKS WITH A LOW CEILING

1196
00:53:09,853 --> 00:53:13,773
IT'S FROZEN, SO YOU MUST BE CAREFUL

1197
00:53:13,857 --> 00:53:15,483
THE FIRST GATEWAY, TONGCHEONMUN

1198
00:53:15,567 --> 00:53:18,361
Watch out for the rocks above you
and any falling icicles.

1199
00:53:18,445 --> 00:53:20,947
Is this some kind of obstacle game?

1200
00:53:21,031 --> 00:53:22,073
Gosh, icicles.

1201
00:53:23,366 --> 00:53:26,578
THEY ENTER

1202
00:53:26,661 --> 00:53:28,455
He's right. There's ice here.

1203
00:53:32,751 --> 00:53:34,044
"The gate to the sky."

1204
00:53:35,378 --> 00:53:36,880
This is nothing.

1205
00:53:38,924 --> 00:53:41,676
TODAY'S ACE, CAR, THE GARDEN,
PASSES WITH EASE

1206
00:53:41,760 --> 00:53:43,595
HE ARRIVES AT THE SKY

1207
00:53:43,678 --> 00:53:44,554
Gosh.

1208
00:53:44,638 --> 00:53:48,058
Gosh, this is like rock climbing.

1209
00:53:48,892 --> 00:53:51,394
STRUGGLING WITH THE STEEP SLOPE

1210
00:53:51,478 --> 00:53:52,312
What is this?

1211
00:53:53,939 --> 00:53:56,107
Damn it!

1212
00:53:57,651 --> 00:53:58,860
GROANS

1213
00:53:58,944 --> 00:54:01,446
DOWOON ARRIVES AT THE SKY TOO

1214
00:54:01,529 --> 00:54:02,364
SHOUTS

1215
00:54:05,367 --> 00:54:06,910
-What is it?
-I hit my head.

1216
00:54:08,536 --> 00:54:10,705
FEELS BAD FOR HIM

1217
00:54:10,789 --> 00:54:11,706
TEARING UP

1218
00:54:11,790 --> 00:54:13,249
Lee Chae-min, watch your head.

1219
00:54:14,250 --> 00:54:15,335
It's very narrow here.

1220
00:54:15,418 --> 00:54:17,170
IT WON'T LET YOU PASS EASILY

1221
00:54:17,253 --> 00:54:18,296
You hit your head?

1222
00:54:18,380 --> 00:54:19,547
I hit my head.

1223
00:54:22,217 --> 00:54:23,134
Your head…

1224
00:54:23,927 --> 00:54:25,887
isn't even that bright to begin with.

1225
00:54:25,971 --> 00:54:28,515
-Hey, don't say that!
-You can't go and hit it.

1226
00:54:29,099 --> 00:54:30,850
I'm not that dumb.

1227
00:54:31,518 --> 00:54:33,478
CHAE-MIN PASSES THROUGH TOO

1228
00:54:33,561 --> 00:54:34,604
AT 1,814 M ABOVE SEA LEVEL

1229
00:54:34,688 --> 00:54:37,816
JUNGSANRI: 5 HOURS, 17 MINUTES
BAEKMUDONG: 5 HOURS, 32 MINUTES

1230
00:54:39,651 --> 00:54:41,319
Yes, be careful here.

1231
00:54:41,403 --> 00:54:44,030
THEY PASS TONGCHEONMUN, THE FIRST GATEWAY

1232
00:54:44,114 --> 00:54:45,699
This is a pretty cool mountain too.

1233
00:54:46,408 --> 00:54:48,159
It's just that I hate climbing it.

1234
00:54:48,243 --> 00:54:49,661
CHEONWANGBONG

1235
00:54:51,579 --> 00:54:52,455
We're almost here.

1236
00:54:52,539 --> 00:54:54,207
Gosh. Really?

1237
00:54:54,290 --> 00:54:56,042
This is last part,
"The Stairway to Heaven."

1238
00:54:56,126 --> 00:54:57,168
I'm going to cry.

1239
00:54:58,420 --> 00:54:59,421
I really will.

1240
00:55:00,046 --> 00:55:01,589
Chae-min, you're almost there.

1241
00:55:02,132 --> 00:55:03,341
You're almost there, Chae-min.

1242
00:55:03,425 --> 00:55:04,843
Yeah, we're almost there, Tarzzan.

1243
00:55:07,262 --> 00:55:13,893
THE SECOND GATEWAY TO CHEONWANGBONG,
THE STAIRWAY TO HEAVEN

1244
00:55:15,603 --> 00:55:19,065
A LONG STRETCH OF STAIRS IN FRONT OF THEM

1245
00:55:21,568 --> 00:55:22,527
Stairs are so tough.

1246
00:55:22,610 --> 00:55:23,862
My goodness.

1247
00:55:28,783 --> 00:55:30,368
Still, stairs are a bit better.

1248
00:55:32,203 --> 00:55:34,205
GOING BACK AND FORTH

1249
00:55:34,289 --> 00:55:39,127
WORKING HARD

1250
00:55:39,210 --> 00:55:40,587
Shall we sprint the homestretch?

1251
00:55:40,670 --> 00:55:41,588
Shall we run?

1252
00:55:41,671 --> 00:55:43,256
-You got the passion, Tarzzan?
-I do.

1253
00:55:43,339 --> 00:55:44,549
Five minutes more?

1254
00:55:44,632 --> 00:55:46,092
Climb up like a flying squirrel.

1255
00:55:46,176 --> 00:55:47,552
IT MEANS HE HIMSELF WON'T RUN

1256
00:55:47,635 --> 00:55:48,595
Five to ten minutes.

1257
00:55:48,678 --> 00:55:50,680
We just need to climb that, right?

1258
00:55:50,764 --> 00:55:51,765
I think so.

1259
00:55:52,932 --> 00:55:53,808
You're almost there.

1260
00:55:53,892 --> 00:55:54,851
The young ones.

1261
00:55:54,934 --> 00:55:55,810
YOUNG CANDIDATE 1

1262
00:55:55,894 --> 00:55:57,020
The young ones.

1263
00:55:57,103 --> 00:55:58,480
YOUNG ONES: DOWOON AND TARZZAN

1264
00:55:58,563 --> 00:55:59,397
Here we go!

1265
00:55:59,481 --> 00:56:02,484
Hold on. Let me eat a <i>jjondeugi</i>.
No, I mean…

1266
00:56:03,068 --> 00:56:04,569
DOWOON EATS TRAIL FOOD UNTIL THE END

1267
00:56:04,652 --> 00:56:05,487
You want one?

1268
00:56:05,570 --> 00:56:06,404
It's okay.

1269
00:56:06,488 --> 00:56:07,322
Take your time.

1270
00:56:07,405 --> 00:56:09,157
TEAM BAEKMUDONG
HAS ENERGY LEFT AND WILL RUN

1271
00:56:09,240 --> 00:56:11,159
Get there quickly
and come back with your car.

1272
00:56:11,242 --> 00:56:12,994
Okay. What?

1273
00:56:13,078 --> 00:56:14,037
What?

1274
00:56:14,120 --> 00:56:16,539
THAT'S OUT OF THE MINISTER
OF TRANSPORT'S CONTROL

1275
00:56:16,623 --> 00:56:19,125
We did all this,
but what if there's something more?

1276
00:56:19,209 --> 00:56:20,794
-Come on.
-No way.

1277
00:56:21,294 --> 00:56:22,170
SNORTS

1278
00:56:22,253 --> 00:56:23,463
Why are you laughing?

1279
00:56:23,546 --> 00:56:25,006
Is it because he knows the truth?

1280
00:56:25,090 --> 00:56:26,508
WHAT DOES THE OMINOUS LAUGH MEAN?

1281
00:56:27,092 --> 00:56:28,301
Let's run now.

1282
00:56:28,384 --> 00:56:30,553
YOUNG TEAM BAEKMUDONG STARTS RUNNING

1283
00:56:31,262 --> 00:56:32,847
FROM TARZZAN'S CAM

1284
00:56:32,931 --> 00:56:35,016
FROM DOWOON'S CAM

1285
00:56:35,100 --> 00:56:38,603
A CLEAN CORNER TURN

1286
00:56:38,686 --> 00:56:42,065
THE DISTANCE GROWS IN AN INSTANT

1287
00:56:42,148 --> 00:56:45,318
BREATHING OUT

1288
00:56:45,401 --> 00:56:48,029
TARZZAN LIVING UP TO HIS NAME

1289
00:56:48,113 --> 00:56:51,157
THE EX-SPECIAL FORCES CAMERAMAN
RUNS WITH A SMILE

1290
00:56:52,158 --> 00:56:54,536
DOWOON CURSES IN ENGLISH

1291
00:56:55,120 --> 00:57:00,166
THE LAST DANCE RUNNING AROUND BIG ROCKS

1292
00:57:00,250 --> 00:57:03,795
MORE STAIRS AFTER THE STONE STAIRS

1293
00:57:03,878 --> 00:57:04,712
GRUNTS

1294
00:57:05,213 --> 00:57:06,047
PANTING

1295
00:57:06,589 --> 00:57:07,924
Damn it!

1296
00:57:08,007 --> 00:57:09,926
RUNS OUT OF ENERGY

1297
00:57:10,009 --> 00:57:12,262
TARZZAN IS EXHAUSTED TOO

1298
00:57:12,345 --> 00:57:13,263
Geez!

1299
00:57:13,888 --> 00:57:15,723
There's a long way to go! Don't run!

1300
00:57:17,475 --> 00:57:19,227
This is only the start.

1301
00:57:19,310 --> 00:57:21,688
-What?
-This is the start. It's goes until there.

1302
00:57:21,771 --> 00:57:23,022
You said we were almost there.

1303
00:57:23,565 --> 00:57:27,735
THE END OF THE STAIRS THEY SAW
WHERE THEY STARTED RUNNING

1304
00:57:29,028 --> 00:57:33,241
THE REMAINING DISTANCE

1305
00:57:33,324 --> 00:57:35,660
DISPIRITED

1306
00:57:35,743 --> 00:57:37,203
Dowoon, we got scammed.

1307
00:57:37,745 --> 00:57:39,205
Yeah, that's why I've collapsed.

1308
00:57:40,457 --> 00:57:42,959
FEELING LETHARGIC

1309
00:57:46,212 --> 00:57:47,589
Someone clearly said,

1310
00:57:47,672 --> 00:57:49,549
"Just climb that, and you're there."

1311
00:57:49,632 --> 00:57:52,385
I said, "Okay,"
and decided to run with Dowoon.

1312
00:57:52,469 --> 00:57:54,137
But then, they said
it was only the start.

1313
00:57:54,220 --> 00:57:57,515
So I thought,
"But they just said this was the end."

1314
00:57:58,349 --> 00:57:59,684
LAUGHING

1315
00:57:59,767 --> 00:58:01,227
We must find the culprit.

1316
00:58:01,311 --> 00:58:03,229
The one who said we were almost there.

1317
00:58:03,813 --> 00:58:05,440
Well, I'm the only one who'd say that.

1318
00:58:05,523 --> 00:58:06,566
RIGHT UNDER TARZZAN'S NOSE

1319
00:58:06,649 --> 00:58:08,610
I was talking about the part above it.

1320
00:58:12,655 --> 00:58:14,657
No wonder why he laughed.

1321
00:58:17,660 --> 00:58:19,579
-Hey, this isn't the end.
-What?

1322
00:58:19,662 --> 00:58:20,538
This isn't the end.

1323
00:58:20,622 --> 00:58:21,456
Where is it then?

1324
00:58:21,539 --> 00:58:22,373
Further up.

1325
00:58:22,457 --> 00:58:23,374
This is the beginning.

1326
00:58:23,458 --> 00:58:24,709
THE OTHER TWO HEAR THE SAD NEWS

1327
00:58:24,792 --> 00:58:27,378
We thought this was it,
so we were having a meeting.

1328
00:58:28,254 --> 00:58:29,088
We should go up.

1329
00:58:29,172 --> 00:58:30,006
Let's go.

1330
00:58:31,674 --> 00:58:36,262
YOUNG TEAM BAEKMUDONG
STARTS HIKING WITH ENERGY AGAIN

1331
00:58:37,972 --> 00:58:39,682
It's not here? Up there?

1332
00:58:40,225 --> 00:58:41,267
So there was more.

1333
00:58:41,976 --> 00:58:42,810
Damn it.

1334
00:58:46,231 --> 00:58:53,071
IT'S STILL TIRING EVEN WHEN YOU GO SLOW

1335
00:58:53,154 --> 00:58:54,239
There's no end to it.

1336
00:58:55,156 --> 00:58:59,494
GOING UP HIGHER AND HIGHER

1337
00:58:59,577 --> 00:59:00,828
We can do it.

1338
00:59:05,708 --> 00:59:07,418
Geez, you knew.

1339
00:59:11,130 --> 00:59:14,342
GONE MAD

1340
00:59:16,344 --> 00:59:17,303
Damn it.

1341
00:59:20,139 --> 00:59:22,308
This is why you shouldn't fool around.

1342
00:59:24,310 --> 00:59:29,148
"HIKE WITHIN YOUR MEANS"
-CAR, THE GARDEN

1343
00:59:31,025 --> 00:59:32,527
This is the crux, Chae-min.

1344
00:59:32,610 --> 00:59:33,444
Right.

1345
00:59:34,362 --> 00:59:37,532
THOSE WHO JUST WALK UP STRUGGLE TOO

1346
00:59:37,615 --> 00:59:42,120
THEY FINALLY REUNITE

1347
00:59:42,203 --> 00:59:43,788
Do you want to take a rest?

1348
00:59:46,332 --> 00:59:48,334
Gosh, the running made me so…

1349
00:59:48,418 --> 00:59:49,252
Aren't you dizzy?

1350
00:59:49,335 --> 00:59:50,253
You must feel drained.

1351
00:59:50,336 --> 00:59:51,796
I thought this was the end.

1352
00:59:51,879 --> 00:59:52,714
Me too.

1353
00:59:52,797 --> 00:59:53,673
REAL FALSE HOPE

1354
00:59:53,756 --> 00:59:56,217
I thought we'd only have to
run up to this part.

1355
00:59:56,301 --> 00:59:58,553
I can't even form my words properly.

1356
00:59:58,636 --> 00:59:59,971
How much do we have left now?

1357
01:00:00,054 --> 01:00:00,888
This is crazy.

1358
01:00:01,472 --> 01:00:03,391
200 M TO CHEONWANGBONG

1359
01:00:03,474 --> 01:00:08,813
CURRENT LOCATION, CHEONWANGBONG

1360
01:00:09,480 --> 01:00:13,985
THE REAL HOMESTRETCH

1361
01:00:14,068 --> 01:00:15,695
THE FINAL HIKE LINEUP

1362
01:00:15,778 --> 01:00:17,447
LEAD: TARZZAN

1363
01:00:17,530 --> 01:00:19,699
MIDDLE 1: CAR, THE GARDEN

1364
01:00:19,782 --> 01:00:21,576
MIDDLE 2: DOWOON

1365
01:00:21,659 --> 01:00:24,245
TAIL: CHAE-MIN

1366
01:00:24,787 --> 01:00:25,705
Gosh.

1367
01:00:26,372 --> 01:00:27,290
I see it.

1368
01:00:27,915 --> 01:00:29,667
The final hike!

1369
01:00:30,376 --> 01:00:32,670
Don't trust it.
That might not be the end either.

1370
01:00:33,546 --> 01:00:34,756
DESCEND CLUB'S

1371
01:00:34,839 --> 01:00:35,923
<i>We're here.</i>

1372
01:00:37,133 --> 01:00:38,301
FINAL HIKE

1373
01:00:38,384 --> 01:00:39,302
<i>Okay.</i>

1374
01:00:42,639 --> 01:00:43,556
<i>Are we really here?</i>

1375
01:00:43,640 --> 01:00:45,433
THEY TAKE THEIR FINAL STEPS

1376
01:00:45,516 --> 01:00:47,727
TO THE LAST PEAK

1377
01:00:47,810 --> 01:00:48,811
<i>We're almost there.</i>

1378
01:00:49,854 --> 01:00:53,191
DOWOON, CHAE-MIN, CAR, THE GARDEN, TARZZAN

1379
01:00:53,274 --> 01:00:54,567
Yes!

1380
01:00:57,654 --> 01:01:01,574
ROARING AS IF HE CLIMBED MOUNT EVEREST

1381
01:01:01,658 --> 01:01:05,203
PRESIDENT TAR IS FIRST
TO REACH CHEONWANGBONG

1382
01:01:05,286 --> 01:01:07,038
HUGS THE SUMMIT MARKER

1383
01:01:07,121 --> 01:01:10,083
CAR, THE GARDEN, WHO'S IMPROVED
BY LEAPS AND BOUNDS, ARRIVES

1384
01:01:10,166 --> 01:01:11,584
Where is this place?

1385
01:01:12,126 --> 01:01:13,294
Guys.

1386
01:01:13,378 --> 01:01:16,255
CHAE-MIN HAD A HARD TIME TODAY
AND ARRIVES WITH MUCH DIFFICULTY

1387
01:01:16,339 --> 01:01:17,173
Gosh.

1388
01:01:18,549 --> 01:01:19,717
Let's go, Dowoon!

1389
01:01:25,014 --> 01:01:28,434
LASTLY, DOWOON ARRIVES

1390
01:01:29,435 --> 01:01:35,817
EVERYONE HAS ARRIVED AT CHEONWANGBONG

1391
01:01:35,900 --> 01:01:37,652
The final quest.

1392
01:01:38,152 --> 01:01:39,821
The sacred mountain of the Korean people.

1393
01:01:39,904 --> 01:01:43,783
You've successfully climbed
to Cheonwangbong of Jirisan.

1394
01:01:43,866 --> 01:01:45,118
Congratulations!

1395
01:01:45,201 --> 01:01:49,372
CHEONWANGBONG

1396
01:01:49,455 --> 01:01:53,751
THE PLACE WHERE THE CLOUDS REST
AND THE WIND REACHES FIRST

1397
01:01:55,795 --> 01:02:02,260
WITH ITS COUNTLESS RIDGES AND VALLEYS

1398
01:02:02,343 --> 01:02:06,514
IT IS THE SACRED MOUNTAIN
OF THE KOREAN PEOPLE

1399
01:02:06,597 --> 01:02:10,601
THE KOREAN SPIRIT AROSE FROM HERE

1400
01:02:10,685 --> 01:02:13,646
THE PLACE ABOVE THE CLOUDS
AND CLOSEST TO THE SKY

1401
01:02:15,773 --> 01:02:20,236
THE HIGHEST PEAK OF JIRISAN
AT 1,915 M ABOVE SEA LEVEL

1402
01:02:21,362 --> 01:02:24,198
THEY HAVE SUCCESSFULLY CLIMBED
TO CHEONWANGBONG, JIRISAN

1403
01:02:25,700 --> 01:02:26,784
That was the last hike.

1404
01:02:26,868 --> 01:02:27,702
Good job, everyone.

1405
01:02:27,785 --> 01:02:29,162
Good job.

1406
01:02:29,245 --> 01:02:31,080
EXHAUSTED

1407
01:02:31,664 --> 01:02:34,000
Congratulations
on the last hike of our lives.

1408
01:02:34,625 --> 01:02:36,127
This was our last hike ever.

1409
01:02:36,669 --> 01:02:38,880
NO ENERGY LEFT TO SPEAK

1410
01:02:38,963 --> 01:02:41,132
It's a bit cloudy, so you can't see.

1411
01:02:41,215 --> 01:02:43,259
But usually,
there's a very cool sea of clouds.

1412
01:02:43,801 --> 01:02:45,845
And a lot of people come
to see the sunrise.

1413
01:02:45,928 --> 01:02:47,013
I see.

1414
01:02:47,680 --> 01:02:51,851
IT'S A PITY THAT TODAY IS CLOUDY

1415
01:02:51,934 --> 01:02:54,729
BUT ON SUNNY DAYS, YOU CAN CLEARLY SEE

1416
01:02:54,812 --> 01:02:58,191
THE OUTLINE OF THE MOUNTAINS
IN THE DISTANCE

1417
01:02:58,274 --> 01:03:00,318
ALSO

1418
01:03:00,401 --> 01:03:04,697
ALONG WITH THE SPECTACULAR SCENE
CREATED BY THE ROLLING SEA OF CLOUDS

1419
01:03:07,450 --> 01:03:11,329
YOU CAN SEE THE BEAUTIFUL SUNRISE

1420
01:03:22,715 --> 01:03:29,639
SADLY, THEY CAN'T SEE IT TODAY

1421
01:03:31,015 --> 01:03:33,684
The view was a bit of a shame.

1422
01:03:33,768 --> 01:03:37,146
Compared to how difficult it was,
the view was a bit disappointing.

1423
01:03:37,730 --> 01:03:39,273
It wasn't worth the effort at all.

1424
01:03:40,733 --> 01:03:42,944
STILL, HE CAN'T MISS OUT
ON TAKING PHOTOS NOW

1425
01:03:43,027 --> 01:03:46,489
<i>Still, when you reach the top,</i>
<i>it feels like the end.</i>

1426
01:03:46,572 --> 01:03:47,573
<i>That was nice.</i>

1427
01:03:47,657 --> 01:03:49,992
CHAE-MIN ALSO TAKES PHOTOS
OF THE SUMMIT MARKER

1428
01:03:50,076 --> 01:03:53,454
<i>I really enjoyed the beauty</i>
<i>of a snowy mountain.</i>

1429
01:03:54,205 --> 01:03:57,583
The sky was a bit foggy and cloudy,

1430
01:03:57,667 --> 01:03:59,669
so it didn't feel open and refreshing.

1431
01:03:59,752 --> 01:04:00,962
That was a bit of a shame.

1432
01:04:04,048 --> 01:04:08,845
AFTER RUNNING,
DOWOON JUST LIES DOWN

1433
01:04:08,928 --> 01:04:12,390
<i>This sickening show</i>
<i>has finally come to an end.</i>

1434
01:04:13,766 --> 01:04:16,769
Gosh, so many people
are going to be freed now.

1435
01:04:17,353 --> 01:04:19,480
Honestly, aren't you all happy too?

1436
01:04:20,398 --> 01:04:22,525
I bet our camera operators
are happier than we are.

1437
01:04:25,361 --> 01:04:28,739
TARZZAN'S HAIR IS AN ABSOLUTE MESS

1438
01:04:28,823 --> 01:04:30,825
Today was the toughest.

1439
01:04:30,908 --> 01:04:34,370
I shouldn't have fooled around
and run in the middle.

1440
01:04:36,497 --> 01:04:37,874
LAUGHING IN REGRET

1441
01:04:37,957 --> 01:04:40,501
Everything became a mess from that point.

1442
01:04:41,711 --> 01:04:44,630
Simply because it was Jirisan,

1443
01:04:44,714 --> 01:04:47,592
that in itself was meaningful.

1444
01:04:47,675 --> 01:04:51,095
THEY TAKE A PHOTO
OF THE LAST SUMMIT MARKER

1445
01:04:51,178 --> 01:04:53,055
-Here we go.
-Get closer to the summit marker.

1446
01:04:53,139 --> 01:04:54,181
Look at this camera.

1447
01:04:54,265 --> 01:04:55,308
Here we go.

1448
01:04:55,975 --> 01:04:57,101
We'll take some more.

1449
01:05:02,148 --> 01:05:04,150
Okay, we've taken the ones
with just the members.

1450
01:05:05,401 --> 01:05:07,612
CHEONWANGBONG, JIRISAN

1451
01:05:07,695 --> 01:05:09,947
MARCH 12, 2026
THE LAST CLIMB OF DESCEND CLUB

1452
01:05:10,990 --> 01:05:13,326
The sun suddenly came out.

1453
01:05:21,250 --> 01:05:25,129
CHEONWANGBONG, JIRISAN, SUCCESS

1454
01:05:25,212 --> 01:05:28,633
TAEBAEKSAN, SEORAKSAN, HALLASAN,
THE YEONGNAM ALPS, JIRISAN

1455
01:05:30,259 --> 01:05:31,552
ONLY LEFT WITH THE DESCENT

1456
01:05:34,138 --> 01:05:35,348
DESCEND CLUB'S FINAL DESCENT

1457
01:05:35,431 --> 01:05:37,934
CHEONWANGBONG

1458
01:05:38,017 --> 01:05:40,269
THE SUNDURYU TRAIL TAKES ABOUT 3 HOURS

1459
01:05:40,353 --> 01:05:41,687
CHEONWANBGONG, BEOPGYESA

1460
01:05:41,771 --> 01:05:42,939
GRADIENT 31.8%

1461
01:05:43,022 --> 01:05:45,483
THEIR STEEPEST SLOPE EVER

1462
01:05:45,566 --> 01:05:47,985
CHEONWANGBONG

1463
01:05:48,069 --> 01:05:50,488
IT DESCENDS STRAIGHT DOWN
FROM THE BEGINNING

1464
01:05:51,906 --> 01:05:55,368
THEIR FIRST TIME FACING
EXTREMELY HARD DIFFICULTY LEVEL

1465
01:05:55,993 --> 01:05:57,453
This place was the worst.

1466
01:05:59,080 --> 01:05:59,914
It was just…

1467
01:06:00,665 --> 01:06:02,625
It was a lot harder
than the other mountains.

1468
01:06:04,210 --> 01:06:05,795
VERY STEEP SCREE TRAIL

1469
01:06:05,878 --> 01:06:08,130
VERY STEEP STAIRS

1470
01:06:08,214 --> 01:06:10,424
VERY STEEP ICY PATHS

1471
01:06:10,508 --> 01:06:11,968
VERY STEEP ROCKY PATHS

1472
01:06:12,051 --> 01:06:13,386
YOU CAN'T LET YOUR GUARD DOWN

1473
01:06:13,469 --> 01:06:14,387
Let's not shoot it.

1474
01:06:14,470 --> 01:06:15,846
It's dangerous here.

1475
01:06:15,930 --> 01:06:17,598
One, two, three.

1476
01:06:18,391 --> 01:06:20,851
FOR THE FIRST TIME ON TAKE A HIKE!,
THEY GIVE UP FILMING

1477
01:06:20,935 --> 01:06:23,145
The camera operators are gone.

1478
01:06:23,229 --> 01:06:24,855
You're right.

1479
01:06:24,939 --> 01:06:28,776
HERE'S FOOTAGE FROM CAMERAS
ON THE CASTS' BAGS

1480
01:06:29,402 --> 01:06:31,946
THEY START THE DESCENT

1481
01:06:32,530 --> 01:06:33,823
-Gosh, this is…
-Let's go.

1482
01:06:33,906 --> 01:06:34,824
This is scary.

1483
01:06:36,075 --> 01:06:37,660
Don't scare me like that.

1484
01:06:38,369 --> 01:06:39,203
Gosh.

1485
01:06:40,246 --> 01:06:41,706
SCARILY STEEP

1486
01:06:41,789 --> 01:06:42,957
Gosh, this is…

1487
01:06:43,541 --> 01:06:44,667
It's slippery here.

1488
01:06:45,376 --> 01:06:47,294
LEADING THE DESCENT GARDEN IS KIND

1489
01:06:47,378 --> 01:06:48,671
Hold on. Geez.

1490
01:06:49,296 --> 01:06:51,424
TRAFFIC JAM

1491
01:06:51,507 --> 01:06:53,092
It's too steep here.

1492
01:06:54,635 --> 01:06:56,721
HOLDING ROCKS
INSTEAD OF HIKING POLES AS THEY MOVE

1493
01:07:01,851 --> 01:07:02,727
Let's go home!

1494
01:07:02,810 --> 01:07:04,103
THEY BARELY ESCAPE CHEONWANGBONG

1495
01:07:05,104 --> 01:07:07,732
It hurts a little less today.

1496
01:07:09,400 --> 01:07:11,027
Maybe it's because we haven't begun yet.

1497
01:07:11,110 --> 01:07:11,944
You think so?

1498
01:07:12,028 --> 01:07:14,989
A STEEP SCREE TRAIL BEGINS IMMEDIATELY

1499
01:07:15,823 --> 01:07:17,324
Descending here is like…

1500
01:07:17,408 --> 01:07:18,492
THUMP

1501
01:07:18,576 --> 01:07:20,036
This is rock climbing.

1502
01:07:20,119 --> 01:07:22,204
This is pretty wild.

1503
01:07:22,288 --> 01:07:24,165
THE ROCK SIZES MAKE IT HARD
TO TAKE A STEP

1504
01:07:24,248 --> 01:07:26,000
I feel like I need to
descend on all fours.

1505
01:07:26,709 --> 01:07:29,795
GOING DOWN ON ALL FOURS

1506
01:07:29,879 --> 01:07:31,672
Why am I going down this way?

1507
01:07:31,756 --> 01:07:32,590
FROM CHAE-MIN'S CAM

1508
01:07:32,673 --> 01:07:33,507
Be careful.

1509
01:07:33,591 --> 01:07:34,425
Okay.

1510
01:07:35,634 --> 01:07:38,554
This has to be the hardest descent trail.

1511
01:07:38,637 --> 01:07:41,223
MOST DIFFICULT DESCENT TRAIL,
AS CHOSEN BY DESCEND CLUB

1512
01:07:41,307 --> 01:07:43,225
SHORTEST TRAIL TO CHEONWANGBONG

1513
01:07:43,309 --> 01:07:45,269
BUT ALSO MEANS THE GRADIENT IS VERY STEEP

1514
01:07:46,187 --> 01:07:48,022
This wasn't meant for people to climb up.

1515
01:07:48,522 --> 01:07:49,356
FROM TARZZAN'S CAM

1516
01:07:49,440 --> 01:07:51,067
GOING DOWN A PATH HARD TO EVEN CLIMB

1517
01:07:51,150 --> 01:07:51,984
Geez.

1518
01:07:53,444 --> 01:07:54,278
Gosh!

1519
01:07:54,862 --> 01:07:55,780
Goodness.

1520
01:07:55,863 --> 01:07:57,448
-Hey.
-That was close.

1521
01:07:58,616 --> 01:07:59,450
Be careful.

1522
01:08:01,327 --> 01:08:02,161
Holy…

1523
01:08:04,747 --> 01:08:06,373
I just got chills down my spine.

1524
01:08:07,208 --> 01:08:09,001
WHY DID YOU SLIP A LOT ON YOUR WAY DOWN?

1525
01:08:09,085 --> 01:08:10,711
There were rocks everywhere.

1526
01:08:10,795 --> 01:08:14,298
Mud, rock, mud, rock.
It kept going back and forth.

1527
01:08:14,381 --> 01:08:16,967
I guess I got tired there early.

1528
01:08:17,676 --> 01:08:21,639
"Jirisan? It'll be nothing."
That's what I had thought.

1529
01:08:22,890 --> 01:08:24,475
But I lost.

1530
01:08:29,063 --> 01:08:31,482
THE OLDER MEMBERS ARE TIRED TOO

1531
01:08:32,191 --> 01:08:33,067
Seriously, Dowoon.

1532
01:08:33,609 --> 01:08:35,402
-Yeah?
-I hate going down too.

1533
01:08:36,654 --> 01:08:38,447
The stairs are very steep.

1534
01:08:38,531 --> 01:08:39,365
Be careful.

1535
01:08:39,448 --> 01:08:40,741
Gosh, I'm getting acrophobia.

1536
01:08:40,825 --> 01:08:42,201
THIS TIME, DOWN SOME STEEP STAIRS

1537
01:08:43,494 --> 01:08:44,328
Goodness.

1538
01:08:44,411 --> 01:08:46,664
STEEL STAIRS WITH A CLEAR VIEW BELOW

1539
01:08:48,374 --> 01:08:49,625
Damn.

1540
01:08:49,708 --> 01:08:52,294
WITH HIS FEAR OF HEIGHTS,
IT'S THE HARDEST PART FOR TARZZAN

1541
01:08:53,420 --> 01:08:56,715
HOLDS ONTO THE RAIL TIGHTLY
AND RESUMES WALKING

1542
01:09:01,387 --> 01:09:02,221
What is this?

1543
01:09:02,805 --> 01:09:05,307
HE WALKS DOWN QUICKLY
WHILE LOOKING ONLY AT HIS FEET

1544
01:09:05,391 --> 01:09:07,977
EVERYONE PASSES BY SAFELY

1545
01:09:08,811 --> 01:09:10,229
Gosh, someone's coming up here.

1546
01:09:10,813 --> 01:09:13,190
THEY PAUSE FOR A WHILE

1547
01:09:13,274 --> 01:09:15,109
Why are you hiking up the mountain?

1548
01:09:15,192 --> 01:09:16,569
We're entering the military soon.

1549
01:09:16,652 --> 01:09:18,571
HE ASKS RIGHT AWAY WHY THEY ARE HIKING

1550
01:09:18,654 --> 01:09:19,947
SURPRISED

1551
01:09:20,030 --> 01:09:20,906
Hello.

1552
01:09:20,990 --> 01:09:23,200
THE FRIENDLIEST CELEBRITY
TO RUN INTO ON A MOUNTAIN

1553
01:09:23,284 --> 01:09:24,785
-You must've just turned 20.
-Yes.

1554
01:09:24,869 --> 01:09:27,913
You came hiking
because you'll join the military soon?

1555
01:09:27,997 --> 01:09:29,957
You guys will be in trouble up there.

1556
01:09:30,040 --> 01:09:31,208
You're almost there.

1557
01:09:31,292 --> 01:09:33,460
DESCEND CLUB'S WAY OF CHEERING THEM ON

1558
01:09:33,544 --> 01:09:34,712
Going to the military?

1559
01:09:35,838 --> 01:09:37,381
Tarzzan, they're younger than you.

1560
01:09:37,464 --> 01:09:39,466
I'm halfway to 50.

1561
01:09:40,050 --> 01:09:41,343
TARZZAN, 25
THE CLUB'S YOUNGEST

1562
01:09:41,427 --> 01:09:42,511
Goodness.

1563
01:09:42,595 --> 01:09:43,804
You're tired?

1564
01:09:43,888 --> 01:09:45,472
It's not like the old days anymore.

1565
01:09:45,556 --> 01:09:46,807
THEY PASS THE STEEP STAIRS

1566
01:09:46,891 --> 01:09:49,476
ROTARI SHELTER
CURRENT LOCATION

1567
01:09:49,560 --> 01:09:50,728
It's nice here.

1568
01:09:51,395 --> 01:09:52,396
1 HOUR, 28 MINUTES PASSED

1569
01:09:52,479 --> 01:09:53,772
ROTARI SHELTER

1570
01:09:54,648 --> 01:09:56,901
THE LAST TASTE OF TRAIL FOOD

1571
01:09:58,611 --> 01:10:00,070
YUM

1572
01:10:00,154 --> 01:10:02,323
REPLENISHING ENERGY WITH PRECIOUS SNACKS

1573
01:10:03,032 --> 01:10:06,076
The snowflakes are pretty.

1574
01:10:06,994 --> 01:10:09,121
IT GRADUALLY STARTS TO SNOW

1575
01:10:09,205 --> 01:10:11,332
THEY FINISH THEIR SHORT REST

1576
01:10:11,916 --> 01:10:12,917
Shall we go?

1577
01:10:13,751 --> 01:10:14,960
Does it get a bit better now?

1578
01:10:15,044 --> 01:10:16,253
1 HOUR 40 MINUTES PASSED

1579
01:10:16,337 --> 01:10:17,671
THEY RESUME DESCENT

1580
01:10:17,755 --> 01:10:20,382
Honestly, it'd be awesome
if the gradient just goes down.

1581
01:10:20,466 --> 01:10:23,969
AS SOON AS THEY RESUME WALKING

1582
01:10:24,053 --> 01:10:27,348
THE SNOW GETS HEAVIER

1583
01:10:28,182 --> 01:10:29,225
It's snowing a lot.

1584
01:10:30,559 --> 01:10:31,810
The weather forecast was right.

1585
01:10:38,692 --> 01:10:41,153
It snowed on the first day on Seoraksan,
and on the last day…

1586
01:10:41,237 --> 01:10:42,947
President Tar, anything you'd like to say?

1587
01:10:43,530 --> 01:10:44,615
Shall we hurry down?

1588
01:10:45,532 --> 01:10:48,661
THE DOCENT IS THE ONLY ONE
FEELING SENTIMENTAL

1589
01:10:50,412 --> 01:10:52,081
It does look pretty in the snow.

1590
01:10:55,834 --> 01:10:57,086
We should hurry down.

1591
01:10:58,254 --> 01:10:59,171
DESCENDING QUICKLY

1592
01:10:59,255 --> 01:11:00,923
-We might turn into snowmen.
-Yeah.

1593
01:11:01,924 --> 01:11:02,841
It's snowing a lot.

1594
01:11:03,384 --> 01:11:05,219
I've never seen so much snow this year.

1595
01:11:05,302 --> 01:11:07,554
I know.
Seoul didn't snow this much either.

1596
01:11:08,097 --> 01:11:09,974
So this is how snow piles up here.

1597
01:11:11,141 --> 01:11:12,059
FROM TARZZAN'S CAM

1598
01:11:12,142 --> 01:11:13,352
Gosh.

1599
01:11:13,435 --> 01:11:17,690
FILMING WHILE MESMERIZED

1600
01:11:19,692 --> 01:11:22,820
PILING UP ON HIS HEAD

1601
01:11:23,862 --> 01:11:25,572
It's snowing at the end.

1602
01:11:25,656 --> 01:11:27,741
DOCENT'S 2ND ATTEMPT

1603
01:11:27,825 --> 01:11:30,327
Even until the finale…

1604
01:11:33,247 --> 01:11:35,791
The difficult trail was one thing.

1605
01:11:35,874 --> 01:11:37,042
But the fact that it snowed…

1606
01:11:38,836 --> 01:11:41,171
The mountain didn't let us
go easily until the very end.

1607
01:11:41,880 --> 01:11:44,049
CLENCHING HIS EYES SHUT

1608
01:11:44,133 --> 01:11:47,052
I felt the mountain was being too clingy.

1609
01:11:48,595 --> 01:11:51,348
The snow makes it slippery. Be careful.

1610
01:11:52,725 --> 01:11:53,684
It's hard to walk here.

1611
01:11:53,767 --> 01:11:55,811
Be careful!

1612
01:11:55,894 --> 01:11:57,438
YOU TOLD US TO BE CAREFUL

1613
01:12:00,024 --> 01:12:02,026
It's this spot.

1614
01:12:03,152 --> 01:12:04,653
Lower your stance a bit.

1615
01:12:04,737 --> 01:12:06,613
LOWERING STANCES BEFORE GOING

1616
01:12:13,287 --> 01:12:15,873
I just skied down.

1617
01:12:17,458 --> 01:12:19,209
It's super slippery here!

1618
01:12:20,169 --> 01:12:21,879
-Here!
-Here.

1619
01:12:21,962 --> 01:12:24,214
WARNING THE LAST PERSON
ABOUT SLIPPING TOO

1620
01:12:26,300 --> 01:12:27,968
Don't step on the ice.

1621
01:12:30,763 --> 01:12:31,972
AIMING FOR THE UNFROZEN EDGE

1622
01:12:32,056 --> 01:12:33,098
He's not like us.

1623
01:12:33,182 --> 01:12:34,975
-He uses his brain.
-Right?

1624
01:12:35,059 --> 01:12:37,019
You and I really are like <i>Dumb and Dumber.</i>

1625
01:12:37,102 --> 01:12:38,020
LAUGHING

1626
01:12:38,103 --> 01:12:39,855
This show sealed it.

1627
01:12:39,938 --> 01:12:41,940
This trail is so…

1628
01:12:42,775 --> 01:12:44,234
The worst mountain for me? Jirisan.

1629
01:12:44,943 --> 01:12:45,819
I mean it.

1630
01:12:45,903 --> 01:12:49,573
Can you briefly tell us how you feel
after your last hike on Jirisan?

1631
01:12:49,656 --> 01:12:51,075
This was the hardest one for me.

1632
01:12:51,658 --> 01:12:53,160
-Harder than Seoraksan?
-Yes.

1633
01:12:53,243 --> 01:12:54,620
I don't know why.

1634
01:12:55,662 --> 01:12:57,164
Maybe it was more psychological.

1635
01:12:57,247 --> 01:12:58,874
But today was the hardest day for me.

1636
01:12:58,957 --> 01:13:00,084
Today was the hardest day?

1637
01:13:01,543 --> 01:13:02,920
Jirisan wasn't easy at all.

1638
01:13:03,003 --> 01:13:04,713
For the first time on the show,

1639
01:13:04,797 --> 01:13:06,423
I found myself swearing.

1640
01:13:06,965 --> 01:13:08,509
I thought, "So this is how it feels."

1641
01:13:09,510 --> 01:13:11,720
Was the toughest mountain Seoraksan?

1642
01:13:11,804 --> 01:13:13,013
No, it was Jirisan…

1643
01:13:13,097 --> 01:13:14,848
Gosh, they were all tough.

1644
01:13:15,432 --> 01:13:16,600
I can't just pick one.

1645
01:13:16,683 --> 01:13:18,727
Everyone, if you want pain,

1646
01:13:19,561 --> 01:13:23,148
just go to the exact same trails
we went to.

1647
01:13:23,982 --> 01:13:26,110
I had a hard time
with the Yeongnam Alps as well.

1648
01:13:27,277 --> 01:13:29,905
Are you sad that it was the last hike?

1649
01:13:29,988 --> 01:13:32,199
Or would you like to
maybe hike one more time?

1650
01:13:32,282 --> 01:13:33,283
Don't be ridiculous.

1651
01:13:34,034 --> 01:13:35,702
I'd appreciate it if you didn't say that.

1652
01:13:36,412 --> 01:13:37,788
I need to speak nicely.

1653
01:13:37,871 --> 01:13:40,332
I'd appreciate it
if you wouldn't say such nonsense.

1654
01:13:40,416 --> 01:13:41,291
I understand.

1655
01:13:42,126 --> 01:13:44,044
<i>Why on earth do you think people hike?</i>

1656
01:13:44,628 --> 01:13:45,587
<i>Do you know now?</i>

1657
01:13:46,547 --> 01:13:48,132
I couldn't find the answer,

1658
01:13:48,632 --> 01:13:52,052
but if I may try to guess
based on my five experiences…

1659
01:13:54,721 --> 01:13:56,932
It's really cliche,
but I think it's this.

1660
01:13:57,015 --> 01:14:01,979
I think a lot of people
want to test themselves.

1661
01:14:02,521 --> 01:14:03,355
The reason is,

1662
01:14:03,981 --> 01:14:05,899
they go there knowing it'll be difficult.

1663
01:14:06,608 --> 01:14:09,570
I think a lot of people go

1664
01:14:09,653 --> 01:14:12,489
to have a fight with themselves.

1665
01:14:12,573 --> 01:14:15,909
I think that's why people hike.

1666
01:14:17,453 --> 01:14:21,123
I'm not totally sure,
but that may be the reason.

1667
01:14:21,206 --> 01:14:22,082
I have no idea.

1668
01:14:22,166 --> 01:14:24,334
I don't think I'll hike
as long as I live. Never.

1669
01:14:25,085 --> 01:14:27,838
In Jeju, someone said

1670
01:14:27,921 --> 01:14:30,966
they wanted to test their limits.

1671
01:14:31,049 --> 01:14:33,719
If you hike with that intent,

1672
01:14:33,802 --> 01:14:36,138
you might feel that kind of joy.

1673
01:14:36,221 --> 01:14:38,932
Like, "I'm going to test
my mental strength."

1674
01:14:40,225 --> 01:14:41,477
When I hike,

1675
01:14:41,977 --> 01:14:44,480
I feel like bad energy is leaving me.

1676
01:14:45,314 --> 01:14:46,982
I don't know why.

1677
01:14:47,065 --> 01:14:49,860
I feel like nothing beats

1678
01:14:49,943 --> 01:14:54,323
the energy you get from nature.

1679
01:14:54,948 --> 01:14:57,451
Yeah, it gives me a lot of good energy.

1680
01:14:57,534 --> 01:14:59,369
-You get a lot of good energy?
-Yes.

1681
01:14:59,953 --> 01:15:02,206
It might've been
because we were a team,

1682
01:15:03,707 --> 01:15:05,959
but as we struggled together on the hikes,

1683
01:15:06,543 --> 01:15:09,004
we became really close
in a short period of time.

1684
01:15:09,671 --> 01:15:10,547
You kind of…

1685
01:15:11,298 --> 01:15:12,716
form a bond of camaraderie.

1686
01:15:13,258 --> 01:15:17,596
It builds stronger relationships
with people.

1687
01:15:17,679 --> 01:15:19,431
RECREATIONAL ACTIVITY THAT BUILDS TEAMWORK

1688
01:15:19,515 --> 01:15:21,475
It may be
a good recreational activity for that.

1689
01:15:21,558 --> 01:15:23,936
So it's worth recommending
for company workshops?

1690
01:15:24,019 --> 01:15:25,979
No, I don't think that's it.

1691
01:15:26,813 --> 01:15:28,482
ALSO

1692
01:15:28,565 --> 01:15:29,441
WITH 100 KM EARNED

1693
01:15:29,525 --> 01:15:32,736
DESCEND CLUB WILL DO A SHOW
THEY WANT TO DO

1694
01:15:34,571 --> 01:15:37,282
<i>Take a Job as a Producer!</i>
Should we change it to this?

1695
01:15:37,866 --> 01:15:41,161
We become the producers,
and you become the cast.

1696
01:15:41,245 --> 01:15:43,038
And we film <i>Take a Hike!</i> again.

1697
01:15:43,121 --> 01:15:44,206
But we'll have to hike too.

1698
01:15:44,289 --> 01:15:45,499
But this time, we won't.

1699
01:15:45,582 --> 01:15:46,667
They'll film themselves.

1700
01:15:46,750 --> 01:15:48,627
HE JUST WANTS REVENGE

1701
01:15:48,710 --> 01:15:51,588
For the game, instead of proverbs,
we'll quiz them on Gen Z slang.

1702
01:15:53,257 --> 01:15:55,092
<i>Take a Camping Trip!</i>

1703
01:15:55,175 --> 01:15:56,677
I question that like hiking.

1704
01:15:56,760 --> 01:15:57,928
I don't get why people camp.

1705
01:15:58,011 --> 01:16:00,931
Going camping in the summer is hell.

1706
01:16:01,014 --> 01:16:02,724
<i>Take a Cycling Trip!</i>

1707
01:16:04,101 --> 01:16:04,935
Please.

1708
01:16:05,018 --> 01:16:08,313
<i>Take a Racing Car Ride!</i>
And make a track…

1709
01:16:09,022 --> 01:16:12,276
Is there a show you'd like to do?

1710
01:16:13,026 --> 01:16:15,404
There is,
but it'd be embarrassing if I told you.

1711
01:16:15,487 --> 01:16:18,240
SILENT

1712
01:16:18,323 --> 01:16:19,992
Should we keep it as a secret?

1713
01:16:20,075 --> 01:16:21,785
SECRET GARDEN

1714
01:16:21,868 --> 01:16:23,829
What you come up with
would be much better.

1715
01:16:23,912 --> 01:16:26,415
I heard what they were discussing earlier.

1716
01:16:26,498 --> 01:16:28,709
What? "Racing Car Ride"?

1717
01:16:28,792 --> 01:16:30,127
-Racing.
-Goodness.

1718
01:16:30,210 --> 01:16:31,211
Don't be ridiculous.

1719
01:16:32,212 --> 01:16:34,548
Places people haven't been to yet.

1720
01:16:34,631 --> 01:16:36,967
We'll go somewhere where we won't suffer.

1721
01:16:37,050 --> 01:16:38,594
<i>Take a Vacation!</i>

1722
01:16:39,344 --> 01:16:40,971
"Why on earth do people take vacations?"

1723
01:16:41,054 --> 01:16:44,683
Why do people pay so much
to go on vacations? I want to find out.

1724
01:16:45,309 --> 01:16:46,977
Honestly, I just want to travel.

1725
01:16:47,644 --> 01:16:48,770
I want to go traveling.

1726
01:16:50,772 --> 01:16:51,607
But for this…

1727
01:16:52,190 --> 01:16:53,275
I've given it some thought.

1728
01:16:53,358 --> 01:16:54,234
Okay.

1729
01:16:55,360 --> 01:16:58,780
If we just do what's fun for us…

1730
01:17:01,241 --> 01:17:02,409
The show would be boring.

1731
01:17:04,244 --> 01:17:05,287
It'd be fun for only us.

1732
01:17:06,538 --> 01:17:10,000
WE HAVE NO IDEA WHAT THEY COULD EVEN DO

1733
01:17:10,083 --> 01:17:12,002
Think it over carefully.

1734
01:17:12,085 --> 01:17:14,421
I mean, Season Two
isn't even confirmed yet.

1735
01:17:14,963 --> 01:17:16,465
Right, we need to see how it goes.

1736
01:17:16,548 --> 01:17:17,841
SORRY FOR JUMPING THE GUN

1737
01:17:18,425 --> 01:17:19,885
It was an honor

1738
01:17:19,968 --> 01:17:21,094
to have worked with you.

1739
01:17:21,178 --> 01:17:22,012
For real.

1740
01:17:22,095 --> 01:17:25,265
Why do you keep talking
as if you're going to disappear?

1741
01:17:25,849 --> 01:17:27,768
You sound like
you're going to cancel the show.

1742
01:17:27,851 --> 01:17:28,935
HIS DREAM: LEAVING THE SHOW

1743
01:17:29,019 --> 01:17:32,856
As president, is there anything
you'd like to say to your fellow members?

1744
01:17:32,939 --> 01:17:34,733
I want to resign as fast as possible

1745
01:17:34,816 --> 01:17:36,401
and start anew.

1746
01:17:38,403 --> 01:17:40,197
Thank you so much for your efforts.

1747
01:17:40,280 --> 01:17:41,114
Thank you.

1748
01:17:45,452 --> 01:17:47,537
THANK YOU FOR WATCHING

1749
01:17:47,621 --> 01:17:50,040
TAKE A HIKE!

1750
01:17:50,123 --> 01:17:57,130
TAKE A…

1751
01:19:11,621 --> 01:19:13,623
Subtitle translation by: Kim Yeeun
